		{"id":"5d9284e604f46d64","type":"text","text":"\n\n# PPJ BUSINESS ENGLISH SPEAKING & LISTENING\n\n## SESSION 4 WORKSHEET — PRIORITY, TIME & DEADLINES\n\nLevel: A1–A2  \nToday’s goal: Bạn có thể sắp xếp công việc, nói về ưu tiên, giải thích chậm tiến độ và trao đổi deadline một cách lịch sự, chân thành và chuyên nghiệp.\n\nNội dung được phát triển từ Chapter 6 — Exploring Daily Habits, đặc biệt là các câu hỏi về lịch hằng ngày, công việc làm vào phút cuối, thói quen trì hoãn và khả năng tự kỷ luật.\n\n# 1. READING — A POLITE AND HONEST DEADLINE UPDATE\n\n## Read the text\n\n### A Busy Day for Mai\n\nMai works in the Import–Export Team. On Monday morning, she has five tasks to finish. \nShe needs to \n- check a packing list, \n- update a shipment report, \n- reply to a supplier, \n- prepare documents for Accounting, \n- and join a meeting at three o’clock.\n\nThe shipment report is the most urgent task because her manager needs it before lunch. \nMai starts with the report. \nShe tells her colleague, “I need to prioritize the shipment report this morning.” \nThe packing list is also important, but it can wait until two o’clock.\n\nAt eleven o’clock, Mai sees that she is **running behind.** \nShe does not stay quiet or wait until the deadline. \nShe sends her manager a clear and polite update.\n\n“I’m sorry, but I need a little more time to complete the report. \nI’m still checking some information with the supplier. \nI’m aiming to finish it by one o’clock. Would that be okay?”\n\nMai is **honest about the delay**, **but she also explains the reason** and **gives a new completion time**. \nHer message is polite, sin-cere, and professional.\n\n**Good workplace communication does not mean saying “yes” to every deadline**. \nIt means ==**giving clear information, showing responsibility, and informing other people early**== when a **plan needs to change**.\n\n## New Vocabulary  \n\n  \n\n|   |   |   |\n|---|---|---|\n|Word / Phrase|Meaning in Vietnamese|Simple Meaning|\n|priority|việc ưu tiên|the most important task|\n|urgent|khẩn cấp|needing quick action|\n|deadline|thời hạn hoàn thành|the time a task must be finished|\n|prioritize|ưu tiên việc quan trọng|decide what to do first|\n|run behind|bị chậm tiến độ|be later than planned|\n|complete|hoàn thành|finish something|\n|delay|sự chậm trễ|something happens later|\n|update|thông tin cập nhật|new information about progress|\n|sincere|chân thành|honest and genuine|\n|professional|chuyên nghiệp|suitable for the workplace|\n|responsibility|trách nhiệm|something you must handle|\n|aim to|đặt mục tiêu làm gì|plan or try to do something|\n\n  \n  \n\n## Multiple-Choice Questions\n\n### 1. Which task is Mai’s first priority?\n\nA. Joining the meeting  \nB. Checking the packing list  \nC. Updating the shipment report  \nD. Preparing documents for Accounting\n\n### 2. Why is the shipment report urgent?\n\nA. The supplier needs it immediately.  \nB. Her manager needs it before lunch.  \nC. Accounting needs it at three o’clock.  \nD. The warehouse cannot find it.\n\n### 3. What can wait until two o’clock?\n\nA. The packing list  \nB. The supplier reply  \nC. The shipment report  \nD. The meeting\n\n### 4. Why is Mai running behind?\n\nA. She arrived late for work.  \nB. She has forgotten the report.  \nC. She is checking information with the supplier.  \nD. She has another meeting.\n\n### 5. What makes Mai’s update professional?\n\nA. She says nothing until the work is finished.  \nB. She blames the supplier for everything.  \nC. She explains the reason and gives a new completion time.  \nD. She asks another person to complete the report.\n\n# 2. CONVERSATION QUESTIONS\n\nWork with a partner. Ask one question, listen to the answer, react, and ask one follow-up question.\n\n|                                                    |                                                          |                                                    |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Conversation Question                              | Meaning in Vietnamese                                    | Specific Workplace Context                         |\n| What is your **first priority** today?             | Ưu tiên đầu tiên của bạn hôm nay là gì?                  | Bạn có nhiều công việc và cần chọn việc làm trước. |\n| Which **task do you need to finish first?**        | Bạn cần hoàn thành công việc nào trước?                  | Hai công việc có deadline khác nhau.               |\n| What are you **aiming to finish** before lunch?    | Bạn đặt mục tiêu hoàn thành việc gì trước giờ trưa?      | Bạn đang lập kế hoạch cho buổi sáng.               |\n| Which task can wait **until the afternoon**?       | Việc nào có thể chờ đến buổi chiều?                      | Một số việc chưa quá khẩn cấp.                     |\n| What is the deadline for this task?                | Thời hạn của công việc này là khi nào?                   | Bạn chưa biết chính xác thời gian phải hoàn thành. |\n| Are you on **s/che/dule** today?                   | Hôm nay bạn có đang đúng tiến độ không?                  | Đồng nghiệp hỏi về tiến độ hiện tại.               |\n| Are you running behind on anything?                | Bạn có đang chậm việc nào không?                         | Bạn cần chia sẻ tình hình một cách chân thành.     |\n| What is causing the delay?                         | Điều gì đang gây ra sự chậm trễ?                         | Một báo cáo chưa thể hoàn thành đúng kế hoạch.     |\n| How much more time do you need?                    | Bạn cần thêm bao nhiêu thời gian?                        | Bạn muốn xin gia hạn deadline.                     |\n| When can you **rea/lis/ti/cal/ly** finish it?      | Thực tế bạn có thể hoàn thành khi nào?                   | Bạn cần đưa ra thời gian mới hợp lý.               |\n| Who needs **an update** from you?                  | Ai đang cần bạn cập nhật thông tin?                      | Manager, supplier hoặc phòng ban khác đang chờ.    |\n| How do you inform someone about a delay politely?  | Bạn thông báo chậm tiến độ một cách lịch sự như thế nào? | Bạn không thể hoàn thành đúng thời hạn ban đầu.    |\n| Do you often leave tasks until the last minute?    | Bạn có thường để công việc đến phút cuối không?          | Bạn nói về thói quen quản lý thời gian.            |\n| What helps you stay on schedule?                   | Điều gì giúp bạn duy trì đúng tiến độ?                   | Bạn chia sẻ một thói quen làm việc hiệu quả.       |\n| What should you do when two tasks are both urgent? | Bạn nên làm gì khi hai công việc đều khẩn cấp?           | Bạn cần trao đổi với manager để xác nhận ưu tiên.  |\n\n## Useful Follow-Up Questions\n\nWhy is that task important?\n\n\nWho is waiting for it?\n\n\nWhat do you need to check first?\n\n\nHow long will it take?\n\n\nWhat will you do after that?\n\n  \n\nCould you finish it today?\n\n  \n\nWhat happens if it is late?\n\n  \n\nHave you informed your manager?\n\n  \n\n## Useful Reactions\n\nThat sounds like a busy day. -> ==S + sounds + like + ....== == (cái gì) đó *nghe có vẻ tương tự* như (cái gì) \n\nThat makes sense.\n\nI see why it is urgent.\n\nThat sounds quite challenging.\n\nI think that is a reasonable plan.\n\nThank you for explaining the situation.\n\nI hope you can finish it on time.\n\n  \n\n# 3. SENTENCE AND COLLOCATION BANK\n\n## A. Talking About Priorities\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Complete Sentence|Meaning in Vietnamese|\n|I need to prioritize the shipment report this morning.|Tôi cần ưu tiên báo cáo lô hàng vào sáng nay.|\n|My first priority is to check the invoice.|Ưu tiên đầu tiên của tôi là kiểm tra hóa đơn.|\n|This task is more urgent than the others.|Công việc này khẩn cấp hơn những việc khác.|\n|I need to finish the packing list first.|Tôi cần hoàn thành packing list trước.|\n|The customer request needs immediate attention.|Yêu cầu của khách hàng cần được xử lý ngay.|\n|I will focus on the urgent documents first.|Tôi sẽ tập trung vào các chứng từ khẩn cấp trước.|\n|Let me check which task has the earliest deadline.|Để tôi kiểm tra công việc nào có deadline sớm nhất.|\n|I think we should handle the shipment issue first.|Tôi nghĩ chúng ta nên xử lý vấn đề lô hàng trước.|\n|Could you confirm which task is the top priority?|Bạn có thể xác nhận công việc nào là ưu tiên cao nhất không?|\n|I have two urgent tasks, so I need to confirm the priority.|Tôi có hai việc khẩn cấp nên cần xác nhận thứ tự ưu tiên.|\n\n## B. Talking About Time and Deadlines\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Complete Sentence|Meaning in Vietnamese|\n|The deadline is three o’clock this afternoon.|Deadline là ba giờ chiều nay.|\n|I’m aiming to finish it before lunch.|Tôi đặt mục tiêu hoàn thành trước giờ trưa.|\n|I should be able to complete it by four o’clock.|Tôi có thể hoàn thành trước bốn giờ.|\n|We need to send the document by the end of the day.|Chúng ta cần gửi chứng từ trước cuối ngày.|\n|I will update you before the meeting.|Tôi sẽ cập nhật cho bạn trước cuộc họp.|\n|Could you send it to me by tomorrow morning?|Bạn có thể gửi cho tôi trước sáng mai không?|\n|We still have two hours before the deadline.|Chúng ta vẫn còn hai giờ trước deadline.|\n|I need about thirty more minutes to finish it.|Tôi cần thêm khoảng ba mươi phút để hoàn thành.|\n|This can wait until tomorrow afternoon.|Việc này có thể chờ đến chiều mai.|\n|We may need to move the deadline to Friday.|Chúng ta có thể cần dời deadline sang thứ Sáu.|\n\n## C. Explaining Progress\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Complete Sentence|Meaning in Vietnamese|\n|I’m still working on the report.|Tôi vẫn đang làm báo cáo.|\n|I have finished the first part.|Tôi đã hoàn thành phần đầu tiên.|\n|I only need to check the final numbers.|Tôi chỉ cần kiểm tra các con số cuối cùng.|\n|The task is almost complete.|Công việc gần hoàn thành rồi.|\n|Everything is going according to plan.|Mọi việc đang diễn ra đúng kế hoạch.|\n|I’m waiting for confirmation from the supplier.|Tôi đang chờ xác nhận từ nhà cung cấp.|\n|I cannot continue until I receive the correct information.|Tôi chưa thể tiếp tục cho đến khi nhận được thông tin đúng.|\n|I’m on schedule at the moment.|Hiện tại tôi đang đúng tiến độ.|\n|I’m a little behind schedule today.|Hôm nay tôi hơi chậm tiến độ.|\n|I will let you know as soon as it is ready.|Tôi sẽ báo bạn ngay khi việc đó hoàn tất.|\n\n## D. Politely Explaining a Delay\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Complete Sentence|Meaning in Vietnamese|\n|I’m sorry, but I need a little more time.|Tôi xin lỗi, nhưng tôi cần thêm một chút thời gian.|\n|I’m running behind because some information is missing.|Tôi đang chậm tiến độ vì thiếu một số thông tin.|\n|There has been a short delay with the supplier confirmation.|Đã có một sự chậm trễ ngắn trong việc xác nhận từ nhà cung cấp.|\n|I may not be able to finish it by two o’clock.|Tôi có thể không hoàn thành được trước hai giờ.|\n|I’m afraid the report will be slightly late.|Tôi e rằng báo cáo sẽ trễ một chút.|\n|I should have informed you earlier.|Lẽ ra tôi nên thông báo cho bạn sớm hơn.|\n|Thank you for your patience and understanding.|Cảm ơn bạn đã kiên nhẫn và thông cảm.|\n|I’m working on it now, and I will send an update soon.|Tôi đang xử lý và sẽ sớm gửi cập nhật.|\n|Could I send the completed file by four o’clock instead?|Tôi có thể gửi file hoàn chỉnh trước bốn giờ thay được không?|\n|I will do my best to avoid any further delay.|Tôi sẽ cố gắng để tránh chậm trễ thêm.|\n\n## E. Responding Politely\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Complete Sentence|Meaning in Vietnamese|\n|Thank you for letting me know early.|Cảm ơn bạn đã thông báo sớm.|\n|I understand the situation.|Tôi hiểu tình hình.|\n|One o’clock is fine for me.|Một giờ là phù hợp với tôi.|\n|Please keep me updated on the progress.|Vui lòng tiếp tục cập nhật tiến độ cho tôi.|\n|Let me know if you need any support.|Hãy cho tôi biết nếu bạn cần hỗ trợ.|\n|Could you send me a quick update at noon?|Bạn có thể gửi cho tôi một cập nhật ngắn vào buổi trưa không?|\n|We can move this task to tomorrow.|Chúng ta có thể chuyển công việc này sang ngày mai.|\n|Please focus on the urgent report first.|Vui lòng tập trung vào báo cáo khẩn cấp trước.|\n|That new deadline sounds reasonable.|Deadline mới đó nghe hợp lý.|\n|Let’s agree on the next step before we continue.|Hãy thống nhất bước tiếp theo trước khi tiếp tục.|\n\n# 4. PATTERNS AND SPEAKING FRAMEWORKS\n\n## Pattern 1 — Explain Your Priority Plan\n\nToday, I need to ______________________________.\n\nMy first priority is ___________________________.\n\nI need to finish it by _________________________.\n\nAfter that, I will _____________________________.\n\nThe task about __________________ can wait until __________________.\n\n### Sample\n\nToday, I need to check three shipment documents. My first priority is the packing list because Warehouse needs it before lunch. After that, I will update the delivery report. The supplier email can wait until the afternoon.\n\n  \n\n## Pattern 2 — Give a Progress Update\n\nI’m currently working on _______________________.\n\nI have already finished ________________________.\n\nI still need to ________________________________.\n\nI’m aiming to finish everything by ______________.\n\nI will update you again at ______________________.\n\n### Sample\n\nI’m currently working on the invoice report. I have already checked the PO numbers. I still need to confirm the quantities. I’m aiming to finish everything by three o’clock. I will update you again at two thirty.\n\n## Pattern 3 — Explain a Delay Politely\n\nI’m sorry, but _________________________________.\n\nI’m running behind because _____________________.\n\nI have already _________________________________.\n\nI still need to ________________________________.\n\nI can realistically finish it by ________________.\n\nWould that be okay?\n\n### Sample\n\nI’m sorry, but I need a little more time. I’m running behind because the supplier has not confirmed the quantity. I have already completed most of the report. I still need to check the final numbers. I can realistically finish it by four o’clock. Would that be okay?\n\n## Pattern 4 — Ask Someone to Confirm a Priority\n\nI currently have two urgent tasks.\n\n  \n\nThe first task is _______________________________.\n\nThe second task is ______________________________.\n\nBoth tasks are due by ___________________________.\n\nCould you confirm which one I should handle first?\n\n### Sample\n\nI currently have two urgent tasks. The first task is the payment report. The second task is the shipment update. Both tasks are due by three o’clock. Could you confirm which one I should handle first?\n\n  \n  \n  \n\n## Pattern 5 — Retell What Happened\n\nUse:\n\nThis morning, __________________________________.\n\nFirst, I _______________________________________.\n\nThen, I ________________________________________.\n\nHowever, _______________________________________.\n\nBecause of that, ________________________________.\n\nSo, I __________________________________________.\n\nFinally, _______________________________________.\n\n### Sample\n\nThis morning, I had five tasks. First, I checked the packing list. Then, I started the shipment report. However, some supplier information was missing. Because of that, I could not finish the report before lunch. So, I informed my manager and asked for more time. Finally, we agreed on a new deadline.\n\n## Pattern 6 — Make a Tomorrow Work Plan\n\nTomorrow, my first task will be _________________.\n\nI need to complete it before ____________________.\n\nNext, I will ___________________________________.\n\nIf I have enough time, I will ___________________.\n\nBefore I leave, I need to _______________________.\n\n### Sample\n\nTomorrow, my first task will be checking the supplier invoices. I need to complete them before lunch. Next, I will prepare the payment report. If I have enough time, I will update the system data. Before I leave, I need to send a short update to my manager.\n\n# 5. CONVERSATION PRACTICE\n\n## Conversation 1 — Five Tasks, Limited Time\n\n### Situation\n\nIt is 9:00 a.m. You have five tasks, but you cannot finish all of them before lunch.\n\n### Your Five Tasks\n\n|   |   |   |\n|---|---|---|\n|Task|Deadline|Importance|\n|Send a shipment report|11:30 a.m.|Very urgent|\n|Check two supplier invoices|12:00 p.m.|Urgent|\n|Reply to a supplier|2:00 p.m.|Important|\n|Update system data|4:00 p.m.|Normal|\n|Prepare tomorrow’s meeting notes|End of the day|Normal|\n\n### Partner A — Staff Member\n\nExplain:\n\n- what you will do first;\n    \n- why it is the first priority;\n    \n- what can wait;\n    \n- when each important task will be finished.\n    \n\nUse:\n\nMy first priority is...\n\nI need to finish it by...\n\nAfter that, I will...\n\nThis task can wait until...\n\nI’m aiming to complete everything by...\n\n### Partner B — Team Leader\n\nAsk:\n\nWhich task will you handle first?\n\nWhy is that your first priority?\n\nWhen can you finish the invoices?\n\nWhich task can wait until the afternoon?\n\nDo you need any support?  \n\n### Your Goal\n\nAgree on a clear work plan for the day.\n\n### Finish With\n\nSo, the first priority is __________________________.\n\nYou will finish it by ______________________________.\n\nAfter that, you will _______________________________.\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n## Conversation 2 — You Cannot Meet the Deadline\n\n### Situation\n\nYou promised to send a report at 2:00 p.m. It is now 1:30 p.m. Some information from the supplier is still missing. You need one more hour.\n\n### Partner A — Report Owner\n\nExplain the situation politely.\n\nUse:\n\nI’m sorry, but I may not be able to finish the report by two o’clock.\n\nI’m still waiting for some information from the supplier.\n\nI have already completed most of the report.\n\nI need about one more hour.\n\nI can send the completed report by three o’clock.\n\nWould that be okay?\n\n### Partner B — Manager or Colleague\n\nRespond professionally.\n\nUse:\n\nThank you for letting me know early.\n\nI understand the situation.\n\nThree o’clock is acceptable.\n\nPlease send me a short update at two thirty.\n\nLet me know if you need any support.  \n\n### Add One Challenge\n\nChoose one:\n\nThe manager needs the report for a meeting at three o’clock.\n\nThe supplier may not reply until two thirty.\n\nAnother urgent task has just arrived.\n\nThe report contains an incorrect quantity.\n\nThe system is not working properly.\n\n  \n  \n  \n\n### Your Goal\n\nComplete the conversation with:\n\n1. a polite explanation;\n    \n2. a clear reason;\n    \n3. a realistic new deadline;\n    \n4. one agreed next action;\n    \n5. a professional closing.\n    \n\n### Closing Sentences\n\nThank you for your understanding.\n\nI’ll keep you updated.\n\nI’ll send it as soon as it is ready.\n\nWe have agreed on three o’clock as the new deadline.\n\nI’ll contact you immediately if anything changes.  \n\n  \n**","x":720,"y":-2713,"width":1100,"height":23175},
