		{"id":"a36fd9d6884aacec","type":"text","text":"\n\n# PPJ BUSINESS ENGLISH SPEAKING & LISTENING\n\n## SESSION 6 WORKSHEET — POLITE REQUESTS & ASKING FOR HELP\n\nLevel: A1–A2  \nHuman theme: Help and cooperation  \nWorkplace theme: Requesting documents and support\n\n## Today’s goal\n\nSau buổi học này, bạn có thể:\n\n- chuyển một yêu cầu trực tiếp thành câu lịch sự và chuyên nghiệp;\n    \n- nhờ đồng nghiệp kiểm tra tài liệu hoặc hỗ trợ công việc;\n    \n- giải thích rõ bạn cần gì, vì sao cần và khi nào cần;\n    \n- phản hồi khi có thể hoặc chưa thể hỗ trợ;\n    \n- phối hợp giữa XNK và TCKT bằng tiếng Anh.\n    \n\n# 1. READING — ASKING FOR HELP PROFESSIONALLY\n\n## Read the text\n\n### A Polite Request Gets Better Support\n\nNam works in the Import–Export Team. \nOn Tuesday morning, he needs to complete a shipment document before *three p.m.* \nHowever, the invoice amount does not match the purchase order.\n\nNam needs help from Hoa in Finance and Accounting. \nHe is busy, so he first thinks about sending a *short message*:\n\n**“Check this invoice now.”**\n\nHowever, Nam understands that this message sounds too direct. \nIt **does not explain the problem or show respect for Hoa’s workload.**\n\nHe changes the message:\n\n“Hi Hoa, could you help me check this invoice when you have a moment? \n*The amount does not match the PO, and we need to complete the shipment documents **before three p.m.*** \nPlease let me know if you need **any additional information.** \nThank you.”\n\nHoa replies:\n\n“Sure. I’m finishing another report now, but I can check it before two p.m. \nCould you send me the PO and the supplier’s invoice?”\n\nNam sends the documents and thanks Hoa for her support.\n\n**A professional request should be clear, polite and re-a-li-stic**. \n- Explain what you need, \n- **why** you need it and **when** you need it. \n- Also remember that the other person **may have their own priorities.**\n\n## New Vocabulary\n\n|                        |                        |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Word / Phrase          | Meaning in Vietnamese  |\n| request                | lời yêu cầu, đề nghị   |\n| support                | sự hỗ trợ              |\n| workload               | khối lượng công việc   |\n| additional information | thông tin bổ sung      |\n| available              | có thời gian, sẵn sàng |\n| realistic              | thực tế, hợp lý        |\n| appreciate             | trân trọng, cảm kích   |\n| urgent                 | khẩn cấp               |\n| check                  | kiểm tra               |\n| attach                 | đính kèm               |\n| forward                | chuyển tiếp            |\n| complete               | hoàn thành             |\n\n## Multiple-Choice Questions\n\n### 1. What problem does Nam find?\n\nA. The supplier is late.  \n**B. The invoice amount does not match the PO.**  \nC. The packing list is missing.  \nD. The system is not working.\n\n### 2. Why does Nam change his first message?\n\nA. It is too long.  \nB. It uses difficult vocabulary.  \n**C. It sounds too direct.**  \nD. It has the wrong deadline.\n\n### 3. When does Nam need to complete the shipment documents?\n\nA. Before noon  \nB. Before two p.m.  \n**C. Before three p.m.**  \nD. Before the end of the week\n\n### 4. What does Hoa ask Nam to send?\n\nA. The packing list and delivery note  \n**B. The PO and supplier’s invoice**  \nC. The GRN and payment report  \nD. The shipment report and contract\n\n### 5. What should a professional request include?\n\nA. Only the deadline  \nB. A strong command  \n**C. What you need, why you need it and when you need it**  \nD. A long explanation of every task\n\n# 2. *COURTESY LADDER*\n\n## Direct → Polite → Collaborative\n\nA direct request is not always grammatically wrong, but it may sound unfriendly or demanding.\n\n### Example 1\n\n**Direct**\n\nCheck this invoice.\n\n**Polite**\n\nCould you check this invoice, please?\n\n**Col-la-bo-ra-tive**\n\nCould you help me check this invoice /**when you have a moment?** /\n**The amount does not match the PO.**\n\n### Example 2\n\n**Direct**\n\nSend me the file today. - /**demand**\n\n**Polite**\n\n**Could you** send me the file today, **please?** - /**request**\n\n**Collaborative**\n\nCould you send me the updated file before **three p.m.?** \n**We need it to complete the shipment documents.**\n\n## A Complete Collaborative Request\n\nUse this structure:\n\n**Friendly opening**\n\n→ Polite request - **COULD YOU PLEASE + [ACTION]\n\n→ Reason **- BECAUSE WE NEED IT TO + [ACTION]\n\n→ Deadline - **AND WE NEED IT BEFORE + [TIME]**\n\n→ Offer information - \n\n→ Appreciation - \n\n  \n\n### Model\n\n*Hi Lan,* \n*could you help me check the invoice when you have a moment?* \n*The amount does not match the PO,* \n*and we need to send the documents before three p.m.* \n*Please let me know if you need any additional information.* \n*Thank you for your support.*\n\n# 3. EXPRESSION BANK\n\n## Function A — Ask for Help\n\n|                                                 |                                                   |                                             |                                         |                    |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Complete Expression                             | Meaning in Vietnamese                             | Connected-Speech Rhythm                     | PPJ Workplace Example                   | Rapid-Fire Trigger |\n| **Could you help me with** + [this invoice]?    | Bạn có thể giúp tôi về hóa đơn này không?         | Could-you HELP me / with-this-invoice?      | XNK cần TCKT kiểm tra invoice.          | Nhờ hỗ trợ.        |\n| **Could you help me check this** [information]? | Bạn có thể giúp tôi kiểm tra thông tin này không? | Could-you-help-me CHECK / this-information? | Hai chứng từ có dữ liệu khác nhau.      | Nhờ kiểm tra.      |\n| **Could you take a look at** [this document]?   | Bạn có thể xem giúp chứng từ này không?           | Could-you-take-a-LOOK / at-this-document?   | Bạn cần đồng nghiệp xem nhanh một file. | Xem giúp.          |\n| **I could use your help with** [this task].     | Tôi cần bạn hỗ trợ công việc này.                 | I-could-use-your-HELP / with-this-task.     | Bạn chưa rõ cách xử lý task.            | Cần hỗ trợ.        |\n\n## Function B — Make a Polite Request\n\n|                                                         |                                                          |                                                 |                                         |                      |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------- |\n| Complete Expression                                     | Meaning in Vietnamese                                    | Connected-Speech Rhythm                         | PPJ Workplace Example                   | Rapid-Fire Trigger   |\n| **Could you send me** the updated file, please?         | Bạn có thể gửi tôi file đã cập nhật không?               | Could-you-SEND me / the-updated-file / please?  | Cần file mới nhất.                      | Xin gửi file.        |\n| **Would you mind checking the** [invoice amount?]       | Bạn có phiền kiểm tra số tiền trên invoice không?        | Would-you-mind CHECKing / the-invoice-amount?   | Invoice và PO không khớp.               | Nhờ kiểm tra amount. |\n| **Could you confirm** [the payment status?]             | Bạn có thể xác nhận trạng thái thanh toán không?         | Could-you-con-FIRM / the-payment-status?        | Supplier hỏi payment.                   | Xác nhận payment.    |\n| **Could you forward** ]the supplier’s] **email to me?** | Bạn có thể chuyển tiếp email của supplier cho tôi không? | Could-you-FORward / the-supplier’s-email-to-me? | Bạn cần xem nội dung trao đổi trước đó. | Chuyển tiếp email.   |\n\n## Function C — Respect the Other Person’s Time\n\n|                                                            |                                                                |                                                         |                                      |                     |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Complete Expression                                        | Meaning in Vietnamese                                          | Connected-Speech Rhythm                                 | PPJ Workplace Example                | Rapid-Fire Trigger  |\n| **When you have a moment**, could you check this?          | Khi bạn có thời gian, bạn có thể kiểm tra giúp không?          | When-you-have-a-MOment / could-you-check-this?          | Task quan trọng nhưng chưa quá khẩn. | Khi rảnh.           |\n| **When you are available**, could we review this together? | Khi bạn có thời gian, chúng ta có thể xem lại cùng nhau không? | When-you’re-a-VAILable / could-we-review-this-together? | Cần phối hợp hai phòng ban.          | Xem cùng nhau.      |\n| **I know you are busy**, but could you help me with this?  | Tôi biết bạn đang bận, nhưng bạn có thể hỗ trợ việc này không? | I-know-you’re-BUSy / but-could-you-help-me-with-this?   | Bạn cần hỗ trợ cho việc khẩn.        | Biết bạn đang bận.  |\n| **Please let me know when you are free.**                  | Vui lòng cho tôi biết khi nào bạn rảnh.                        | Please-let-me-KNOW / when-you’re-free.                  | Cần sắp xếp thời gian trao đổi.      | Hỏi thời gian rảnh. |\n\n## Function D — Explain the Reason and Deadline\n\n|                                                                                     |                                                           |                                                                 |                           |                         |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Complete Expression                                                                 | Meaning in Vietnamese                                     | Connected-Speech Rhythm                                         | PPJ Workplace Example     | Rapid-Fire Trigger      |\n| **We need this** information **to** + [DO SMTHING] complete the shipment documents. | Chúng tôi cần thông tin này để hoàn tất chứng từ lô hàng. | We-need-this-infor-MAtion / to-complete-the-shipment-documents. | XNK cần dữ liệu từ TCKT.  | Giải thích lý do.       |\n| The amount does not match the PO.                                                   | Số tiền không khớp với PO.                                | The-a-MOUNT / doesn’t-match-the-PO.                             | Cần TCKT hỗ trợ kiểm tra. | Amount không khớp.      |\n| **Could you send it** **before** + *[TIME]* three p.m.?                             | Bạn có thể gửi trước ba giờ chiều không?                  | Could-you-SEND it / before-three-p.m.?                          | Có deadline trong ngày.   | Xin trước 3 giờ.        |\n| **We need to finish this before** the shipment is processed.                        | Chúng ta cần hoàn thành trước khi lô hàng được xử lý.     | We-need-to-FINish-this / before-the-shipment-is-processed.      | Chứng từ đang chờ xử lý.  | Nêu deadline nghiệp vụ. |\n\n## Function E — Respond to a Request\n\n|                                                    |                                                        |                                                  |                                    |                       |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| Complete Expression                                | Meaning in Vietnamese                                  | Connected-Speech Rhythm                          | PPJ Workplace Example              | Rapid-Fire Trigger    |\n| Sure, I can help you with that.                    | Được, tôi có thể giúp bạn việc đó.                     | Sure / I-can-HELP you-with-that.                 | Bạn có thể hỗ trợ ngay.            | Đồng ý hỗ trợ.        |\n| I can check it before two p.m.                     | Tôi có thể kiểm tra trước hai giờ.                     | I-can-CHECK it / before-two-p.m.                 | Bạn cần đưa thời gian hoàn thành.  | Nêu thời gian hỗ trợ. |\n| I’m working on another task right now.             | Hiện tại tôi đang làm một công việc khác.              | I’m-WORKing-on-another-task / right-now.         | Bạn chưa thể hỗ trợ ngay.          | Đang bận.             |\n| **Could you send me** the related documents first? | Bạn có thể gửi tôi các chứng từ liên quan trước không? | Could-you-SEND me / the-related-documents-first? | Cần đủ dữ liệu trước khi kiểm tra. | Xin thêm tài liệu.    |\n\n# 4. FIVE SPEAKING PATTERNS\n\n## Pattern 1 — Simple Polite Request\n\n### Framework\n\nCould you help me with __________________, please?\n\n### Sample\n\nCould you help me with this supplier invoice, please?\n\n### Your Turn\n\nCould you help me with ______________________________, please?\n\n## Pattern 2 — Request + Reason\n\n### Framework\n\nCould you ______________________________?\n\nWe need it because ______________________________.\n\n### Sample\n\nCould you check the payment status? We need it because the supplier is asking for an update.\n\n### Your Turn\n\nCould you ______________________________?  \nWe need it because ______________________________.\n\n## Pattern 3 — Request + Deadline\n\n### Framework\n\nWhen you have a moment, could you __________________?\n\nWe need to complete it before __________________.\n\n### Sample\n\nWhen you have a moment, could you check this invoice? We need to complete it before three p.m.\n\n### Your Turn\n\nWhen you have a moment, could you ______________________________?  \nWe need to complete it before ______________________________.\n\n## Pattern 4 — Request + Reason + Support\n\n### Framework\n\nCould you help me ______________________________?\n\nThere seems to be ______________________________.\n\nPlease let me know if you need ______________________________.\n\n### Sample\n\nCould you help me check this invoice? There seems to be a difference between the invoice and the PO. Please let me know if you need the related documents.\n\n### Your Turn\n\nCould you help me ______________________________?  \nThere seems to be ______________________________.  \nPlease let me know if you need ______________________________.\n\n## Pattern 5 — Respond When You Are Busy\n\n### Framework\n\nI’m sorry, but I’m currently working on __________________.\n\nI can help you after __________________.\n\nCould you send me __________________ first?\n\n  \n\n### Sample\n\nI’m sorry, but I’m currently working on a payment report. I can help you after two p.m. Could you send me the PO and invoice first?\n\n### Your Turn\n\nI’m sorry, but I’m currently working on ______________________________.  \nI can help you after ______________________________.  \nCould you send me ______________________________ first?\n\n# 5. TRANSFORM THE REQUESTS\n\nChange each direct sentence into a polite and collaborative request.\n\n## Example\n\n**Direct**\n\nCheck this invoice.\n\n**Collaborative**\n\nCould you help me check this invoice when you have a moment? The amount does not match the PO.\n\n  \n\n### *****1. Send me the PO.*\n\n### *2. Check the invoice amount.*\n\n### 3. Give me the payment status.\n\n### 4. Forward the supplier’s email.\n\n### 5. Fix this information.\n\n### 6. Reply to me before lunch.\n\n### 7. Check the system now.\n\n### 8. Send the updated report today.\n\n### 9. Explain this payment issue.\n\n### 10. Help me finish these documents.\n\n# 6. POLITE INTONATION DRILL\n\nA polite request should sound calm, not like an order.\n\nStress the important word and use a gentle rise at the end.\n\nCould you HELP me with this? ↑\n\nCould you CHECK the invoice, please? ↑\n\nWould you mind SENDing me the file? ↑\n\nWhen you have a MOMENT, could you look at this? ↑\n\nCould you CONFIRM the payment status? ↑\n\nCompare:\n\nToo direct\n\nSend me the file. ↓\n\nPolite\n\nCould you send me the file, please? ↑\n\n# 7. ROLEPLAY — XNK NEEDS TCKT SUPPORT\n\n## Situation\n\nBạn làm việc tại Phòng XNK. Một shipment cần được xử lý trước ba giờ chiều.\n\nBạn phát hiện:\n\n- invoice amount: USD 12,500;\n    \n- PO amount: USD 12,050;\n    \n- supplier is waiting for confirmation;\n    \n- shipment documents must be completed before 3:00 p.m.\n    \n\nBạn cần TCKT hỗ trợ kiểm tra.\n\n## Role A — Import–Export\n\nYour goal:\n\n1. greet your colleague;\n    \n2. explain the mismatch;\n    \n3. ask for help politely;\n    \n4. explain the deadline;\n    \n5. offer to send the documents;\n    \n6. agree on the next action.\n    \n\nUse at least five expressions:\n\nCould you help me check this invoice?\n\nThe amount does not match the PO.\n\nWhen you have a moment, could you take a look at it?\n\nWe need to complete the shipment documents before three p.m.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any additional information.\n\nCould you confirm when you can check it?\n\nThank you for your support.\n\n## Role B — Finance and Accounting\n\nYou are currently preparing a payment report.\n\nYou can check the invoice before 2:15 p.m., but you need:\n\n- the PO;\n    \n- the supplier’s invoice;\n    \n- the supplier’s email;\n    \n- confirmation of the correct currency.\n    \n\nUse at least five expressions:\n\nSure, I can help you with that.\n\nI’m working on another report right now.\n\nI can check it before two fifteen.\n\nCould you send me the PO and invoice first?\n\nCould you also forward the supplier’s email?\n\nPlease confirm the correct currency.\n\nI’ll update you when I finish checking.\n\n## Complete the Conversation\n\n### XNK\n\nHi, could you help me _______________________________________?\n\n### TCKT\n\nSure. What seems to be the problem?\n\n### XNK\n\nThe invoice shows __________________, but the PO shows __________________.\n\n### TCKT\n\nI see. Could you send me ____________________________________?\n\n### XNK\n\nOf course. We need to complete the shipment documents before __________________.\n\n### TCKT\n\nI’m working on __________________________________ right now, but I can check it before __________________.\n\n### XNK\n\nThat would be very helpful. I’ll send you __________________ immediately.\n\n### TCKT\n\nGreat. I’ll update you after I check the documents.\n\n### XNK\n\nThank you for ______________________________________________.\n\n## Final Agreement\n\nComplete:\n\nTCKT will check _____________________________________________.\n\nXNK will send ______________________________________________.\n\nThe checking will be completed before ________________________.\n\nAfter checking, TCKT will ___________________________________.\n\n## Roleplay Success Check\n\n□ I made a polite request.\n\n□ I explained the problem clearly.\n\n□ I gave a reason and deadline.\n\n□ I respected the other person’s workload.\n\n□ I asked what information was needed.\n\n□ We agreed on a clear next action.\n\n□ I thanked my partner politely.\n\n# 8. CONVERSATION PRACTICE — CAN YOU HELP ME?\n\nWork with a new partner.\n\nChoose one situation.\n\n## Situation A\n\nYou need Warehouse to confirm the received quantity.\n\n## Situation B\n\nYou need IT to check a system error.\n\n## Situation C\n\nYou need XNK to send a shipment document.\n\n## Situation D\n\nYou need TCKT to confirm the payment status.\n\n## Situation E\n\nYou need your team leader to review a report.\n\n  \n  \n\nUse this conversation flow:\n\nGreeting\n\n→ Request\n\n→ Problem or reason\n\n→ Deadline\n\n→ Ask for availability\n\n→ Agree on the next action\n\n→ Thank the person\n\n### Support Card\n\nHi, could you help me with __________________?\n\nThere seems to be ______________________________.\n\nWe need to complete it before __________________.\n\nWhen would you be available to check it?\n\nPlease let me know if you need __________________.\n\nThank you for your support.\n\n# 9. DISCUSSION — WHEN SHOULD WE ASK FOR HELP?\n\nChoose four questions.\n\n1. When should you ask for help at work?\n    \n2. Why do some people wait too long before asking?\n    \n3. Is asking for help a sign of weakness?\n    \n4. What information should you include in a request?\n    \n5. How can an unclear request create more work?\n    \n6. When can you say no to a request?\n    \n7. How can you say that you are busy without sounding unfriendly?\n    \n8. Should urgent requests always be handled first?\n    \n9. What makes someone helpful and easy to work with?\n    \n10. Which departments do you ask for help most often?\n    \n\n## Sentence Starters\n\n## I think we should ask for help when...\n\nIn my experience...\n\nOne common problem is...\n\nA good request should include...\n\nIt is difficult to help when...\n\nIf I am busy, I usually say...\n\nOne thing we can improve is...\n\n# 10. FINAL OUTPUT — TRANSFORM 10 DIRECT SENTENCES\n\nYour final challenge is to transform all ten direct sentences into professional requests.\n\nA strong request should include at least two of these elements:\n\n□ Could you...?\n\n□ When you have a moment...\n\n□ Reason\n\n□ Deadline\n\n□ Offer additional information\n\n□ Thank you\n\n## Model Final Answer\n\nDirect\n\nSend me the updated report.\n\nProfessional\n\nWhen you have a moment, could you send me the updated report? We need it for the three o’clock meeting. Thank you for your support.\n\n# 11. HOMEWORK\n\n## Record Five Polite Workplace Requests\n\nRecord five separate requests.\n\nEach request should be approximately 10–20 seconds.\n\n### Request 1 — Ask for a document\n\nCould you _________________________________________________?\n\n### Request 2 — Ask someone to check information\n\nWhen you have a moment, could you __________________________?\n\n### Request 3 — Ask for confirmation\n\nCould you confirm __________________________________________?\n\n### Request 4 — Ask for help with an urgent task\n\nI know you are busy, but could you ___________________________?\n\n### Request 5 — Give a reason and deadline\n\nCould you _________________________________________________?  \nWe need it because _________________________________________.  \nCould you send it before ___________________________________?\n\n# SESSION 6 TAKEAWAY\n\nA professional request is more than:\n\nPlease help me.\n\nUse:\n\nWhat you need + Why you need it + When you need it + Respect for the other person\n\n### Your core sentences\n\nCould you help me with this?\n\nWhen you have a moment, could you check this?\n\nWould you mind sending me the file?\n\nWe need it to complete the shipment documents.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any additional information.\n\nThank you for your support.\n\n**","x":6140,"y":4662,"width":1120,"height":16665},
		{"id":"ef481bd94c9afcfa","type":"text","text":"![[Pasted image 20260730163908.png]]","x":4214,"y":-2520,"width":612,"height":336},
		{"id":"c43d412344043b74","type":"text","text":"![[Pasted image 20260730174448.png]]","x":5356,"y":-2000,"width":340,"height":240},
		{"id":"94d9d057a0c663f2","type":"text","text":"MRS. KATHY:\n\nA GOOD DAY TO ME IS A DAY THAT I GET UP ->\nSEE ALL MEMBERS OF MY FAMILY IS STILL GOING STRONG AND WELL - \nTHEN \nWE WILL GO PLAY PICKLEBALL WITH MY TEAM \n->\nGO TO COMPANY +\nSEE CO-WORKERS + \nCHECK THE REPORTS AND SEE THAT WE MADE A **HUGEEEE SHIPMENTS THAT INCREASE OUR REVENUES**","x":4826,"y":-1698,"width":380,"height":358,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"957d3805ffda9655","type":"text","text":"MS LINDA:\nA GOOD DAY TO ME WOULD BE A DAY THAT I AM NOT TOO BUSY - A DAY THAT I DONT HAVE FULFILL DO TOO MANY PAYMENTS REQUESTS","x":4766,"y":-1311,"width":314,"height":151,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c94e28e1cce8d035","type":"text","text":"MRS ROSA::\nMY GOOD DAY WOULD BE HAVING MORE TIME FOR MYSELF, DOESNT HAVE TOO MANY EMAILS AND QUESTIONS TO REPLY","x":5016,"y":-1110,"width":216,"height":245,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2cb822b5b7361b7f","type":"text","text":"MRS TINA:\n\nA DAY THAT I RECEIVE MY SALARY / PAYMENT \n\n- THE TENTH ÒF EVERY MONTH\n\n","x":5300,"y":-1155,"width":250,"height":191,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"e8f29618067cb807","type":"text","text":"MRS VICTORIA:\nA DAY THAT I HAVE MORE TIME FOR MYSELF - AND MY KIDS ARE **OBEDIENT AND BEING NICE AT HOME**","x":5635,"y":-1083,"width":250,"height":163,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"95130e924119db57","type":"text","text":"MRS HANNAH \nA GOOD DAY IS A DAY THAT \nI GET UP EARLY TO DO EXERCISES, WATER THE TREE -> \nCLEAN THE HOUSE -> \nCOOK BREAKFAST -> \nGO HANGOUT WITH FAMILY + WATCH MOVIES + GO TO CAFES + LISTEN TO MUSIC\n\nAND RELAX - LYING ON MY SOFAS IN THE EVENING \n- AND THAT I RECEIVE MONEY FROM MY HUSBAND ","x":5750,"y":-1770,"width":320,"height":370,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cd52a5536f7a514f","type":"text","text":"MRS RUBY\nA DAY THAT I HAVE TIME TO ENJOY A VACATION WITH MY FAMILY , FRIENDS AND COLLEAGUES  - HAVING GOOD MEAL WITH SEAFOOD (LOBSTERS...)","x":6200,"y":-1509,"width":250,"height":219,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"2f6fd979608a5dfd","type":"text","text":"MS TIFFANY\nA DAY THAT I HAVE MORE TIME TO RELAX, MEET UP WITH MY FRIENDS, WATCH ROM-COM MOVIES, ","x":5810,"y":-1279,"width":260,"height":124,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"5b21f6c35f058ae4","type":"text","text":"MRS VIOLET:\nA WHOLE MONTH THAT I HAVE TIME TO GO ON VACATION WITH MY FAMILY ","x":6120,"y":-1155,"width":250,"height":179,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ddb687e2b7f1029a","type":"text","text":"WHAT IS THE BEST PART OF YOUR DAY?","x":8790,"y":4096,"width":340,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"3fd6ba6fbab6405f","type":"text","text":"![[Pasted image 20260801131307.png]]","x":8400,"y":3269,"width":500,"height":316},
		{"id":"53d47e94c463d4b6","type":"text","text":"### *1. Send me the PO.*\n- .\n- .\n- .\n\n### *2. Check the invoice amount.*\n- .\n- .\n- .","x":5340,"y":13300,"width":359,"height":387},
		{"id":"90e70239cbc7ecac","type":"text","text":"time / moment \n+ activity \n- reason \n\n- feelings","x":7828,"y":4420,"width":160,"height":259,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2eec3e9dd56b0056","type":"text","text":"MRS VICTORIA \nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- EARLY IN THE MORNING EVERYDAY\n- BECAUSE I HAVE MORE TIME FOR MYSELF - I CAN EXERCISE + CLEAN MY HOUSE + RELAX WITH MUSIC","x":8147,"y":3978,"width":305,"height":258,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c3fff0dbd677ed53","type":"text","text":"MRS ANNE:\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- IN THE EVENING \n- WHEN I PLAY WITH MY KIDS AND WATCH MOVIES WITH THEM ","x":8330,"y":4236,"width":320,"height":191,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"73747a31c21b1c13","type":"text","text":"MS TIFFANY:\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- WHEN I HAVE DINNER WITH MY FAMILY\n- BECAUSE I CAN SHARE ABOUT MY DAY \n- EAT MY FAVORITE DISHES","x":8700,"y":4236,"width":285,"height":256,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"e44bd59fc7ad164e","type":"text","text":"MRS VIOLET\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- WHEN I FINISH WORK, I GO HOME AND HAVE DINNER WITH MY FAMILY. THEN I PLAY VIDEO GAMES AND WATCH MOVIES WITH MY FAMILY, OR READ BOOKS TOGETHER\n- IT MAKES ME FEEL RELAXED AND HAPPY","x":9020,"y":4180,"width":380,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8fad75fcfd163676","type":"text","text":"MRS TINA:\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- AT NIGHT\n- BECAUSE I CAN WATCH MOVIES WITH MY KIDS \n\t- AND THAT I CAN COMPLETELY / FULLY RELAX  \n\t- AND THAT I CAN FEEL COMFORTABLE ","x":8513,"y":3780,"width":320,"height":284,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d36f91aa9db41bb7","type":"text","text":"MRS ROSAKY\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- IN THE EVENING \n- BECAUSE I CAN GO SWIMMING, \n- I DONT HAVE TO THINK ABOUT MY WORKS \n\t- AND CAN BE FULLY RELAXED \n- SOMETIMES I TAKE A WALK AROUND MY APARTMENT ","x":8857,"y":3780,"width":480,"height":264,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"06653ed00625bad6","type":"text","text":"MRS HANNAH\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- WEEKEND /SATURDAY NIGHT - BC I DONT HAVE TO DO ANYTHING -  AND I FEEL COMFORTABLE -\n\t- THAT I CAN GO HANG OUT WITH MY FAMILY, \n\t- OR GO TO COFFEE SHOP, \n\t- SOMETIMES I GO GRABBING A MILKTEA  / \n\t- OR SINGING / DOING KARAOKE AT HOME ","x":9337,"y":3956,"width":420,"height":302,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"9d40ef5c1dad79eb","type":"text","text":"THE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS \n- AFTER 11PM - WHEN I FINALLY COME HOME FROM WORKS + SIDE JOB\n- BECAUSE I CAN FOCUS COMPLETELY ON MY HOBBIES\n\t- THAT I CAN PRACTICE DJ-ING\n\t- OR WATCH MOVIES \n\t- OR JUST EXPLORE NEW MUSIC \n\t- SOMETIMES I WOULD TAKE A WALK WITH MY 3 KITTIES - AND CUDDLE MY KITTIES\n\t- STILL - AT WEEKEND - TWICE A MONTH I HAVE TO GET TO MY FRIENDS'S LOUNGE TO HELP THEM AROUND\n- **THIS MAKES ME FEEL THAT AT LEAST I HAVE SOME FREEDOM FOR MYSELF AND MY GF** \n","x":9020,"y":3360,"width":520,"height":451},
		{"id":"f12c51f59aadccbe","type":"text","text":"always put your family at the prioritized list","x":9620,"y":3640,"width":373,"height":60,"color":"5"},
