		{"id":"422746d1f20fd802","type":"text","text":"The best part of my day is ______ because I can ______.","x":7415,"y":7660,"width":378,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d8d9e8eb932433f0","type":"text","text":"It makes me feel ______.","x":7855,"y":7683,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d7298074abe800a9","type":"text","text":"LOVED","x":8136,"y":7926,"width":100,"height":60},
		{"id":"50d017b87849a25f","type":"text","text":"LISTENED","x":8186,"y":7600,"width":120,"height":60},
		{"id":"d670ecb94bc02262","type":"text","text":"RELAXED","x":8216,"y":7776,"width":125,"height":60},
		{"id":"8534d03ad72a13cd","type":"text","text":"JOYFUL","x":8224,"y":7685,"width":101,"height":60},
		{"id":"dcc165f5587c5b22","type":"text","text":"COMFORTABLE","x":8245,"y":7866,"width":160,"height":60},
		{"id":"053b90dd5897def8","type":"text","text":"HAPPY","x":8364,"y":7685,"width":91,"height":60},
		{"id":"b9c46a0e90bb6541","type":"text","text":"MR. MIKE:\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n- VERY SIMPLE : **AROUND 6-7PM** OF **THE 10TH** OF *EVERY MONTH* - BECAUSE I RECEIVE THE SALARY PAYMENT MES-SAGE FROM THE BANK ","x":8760,"y":6320,"width":320,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6b9c722862254085","type":"text","text":"time / moment \n+ activity \n- reason \n\n- feelings","x":7840,"y":7420,"width":160,"height":259,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"039d1c02da72f8a0","type":"text","text":"MRS. LILY \nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n- **IN THE EVENING** \n\t- BECAUSE I HAVE A LOT OF TIME FOR MY FAMILY \n\t\t- I CAN PREPARE DINNER WITH MY CHILDREN \n\t\t-  LISTEN AND SHARE WITH MY KIDS ABOUT OUR DAYS - THIS MAKES ME UNDERSTAND MY KIDS BETTER  ","x":8320,"y":6300,"width":426,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"bb90492af198bec8","type":"text","text":"\nWHAT IS **THE BEST PART** OF YOUR DAY?","x":8740,"y":6700,"width":340,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"26c3f2b3141dd8bd","type":"text","text":"COMP-TỜ-BỒ","x":9218,"y":6520,"width":150,"height":50},
		{"id":"84bf139929d8bfb0","type":"text","text":"MRS TANYA:\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n**IN THE EVENING**\n- AFTER DINNER WITH MY FAMILY \n\t- WE WILL PLAY TOGETHER - WATCH TV TOGETHER - AND SHARE ABOUT OUR DAYS AND WHAT'S SPECIAL ABOUT IT\n- WHEN I LISTEN TO MY CHILDREN - I COULD SEE PARTS OF MY YOUNGER SELF MANY YEARS BEFORE IN THEIR EYES - THIS MAKES ME COMFOR-TA-BLE AND HAPPY ","x":9101,"y":6140,"width":385,"height":360},
		{"id":"b39095181e80f49b","type":"text","text":"MRS SOPHIA\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n- **EARLY IN THE MORNING** - WHEN I WAKE UP AT 5 AM EVERY DAY \n\t- BECAUSE I CAN DO YOGA AT AROUND 5:15 IN THE MORNING \n\t- THEN I HAVE BREAKFAST WITH MY FAMILY AT AROUND 7:00 AM\n- **IN THE EVENING** \n\t- WHEN I CAN \n\t\t- PLAY PICKLEBALL WITH MY FRIENDS \n\t\t- OR HANG-OUT WITH MY FAMILY ","x":7960,"y":6660,"width":420,"height":391,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"860645e62b2fe41f","type":"text","text":"MRS. JENNY\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n- I FEEL COMFORTABLE WHEN I RELAX WITH A CUP OF COFFEE ***EVERY MORNING*** \n- AND **WHEN I FINISH WORKS ON TIME** \n- ***IN THE EVENING*** WHEN I HAVE MORE TIME TO PLAY WITH MY FAMILY, SUCH AS - SOCCER / OR WATCH TV TOGETHER \n\t- OR **WHEN I HAVE TIME TO HAVE LUNCH** AND DO THE HOUSEWORK TOGETHER \n\t- AND **WHEN I HAVE TIME TO IMPROVE MY ENGLISH SKILLS** \n\t- AND I DO SKIN CARE / APPLY SKINCARE PRODUCTS ","x":8410,"y":6893,"width":500,"height":365,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"bb66cbc6287af382","type":"text","text":"MRS. LUNA\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n- WHEN I HAVE DINNER WITH MY FAMILY ***AFTER COMING BACK HOME***\n\t- BECAUSE I CAN HAVE TIME TO WATCH THE NEWS ON TV\n\t- THEN I GO TO MY MOM'S HOUSE - NEAR MY HOUSE \n\t- THEN I COME BACK HOME AND RELAX WITH MUSIC \n- **SOME AFTERNOONS**, I WOULD HAVE TIME TO PLAY PICKLEBALL WITH MY FRIENDS","x":8920,"y":6893,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0c68e9cc2f490f3f","type":"text","text":"MRS. MARRY\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n- IS ***THE EARLY MORNING*** BECAUSE I CAN ENJOY MY COFFEE AND LISTEN TO MY FAVORITE SONGS OR WATCH SOME NEWS(PAPER)\n\t- THIS IS HOW I USUALLY START A NEW DAY \n\t- IT MAKES ME FEEL RELAXED AND ENERGETIC FOR WORK AND GIVE BETTER SUPPORT \n- HOWEVER - I ALSO LIKE ***LATE AFTERNOONS***, WHEN I SOMETIMES PLAY PICKLEBALL WITH MY TEAM BECAUSE IT HELPS ME ***STAY FIT AND HEALTHY***\n- AND I ALSO **ENJOY THE EVENING** WHEN I HAVE DINNER WITH MY FAMILY\n\t- AFTER THAT I WATCH TV / MOVIES WITH MY HUSBAND BECAUSE WE HAVE SAME INTERESTS","x":9320,"y":6826,"width":420,"height":500,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f45591de8491127f","type":"text","text":"MRS SUNNY:\nTHE BEST PART OF MY DAY IS:\n**EARLY IN THE MORNING**\n- WHEN I WAKE UP TO MY SON'S SMILES \n- OR WHEN WE RIDE BICYCLE AND WATCH THE SUNRISE TOGETHER \n- THIS MAKES ME VERY HAPPY AND ENERGETIC AT THE START OF EVERYDAY ","x":9368,"y":6570,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"d947e93826ffa0e5","type":"text","text":"homework 3: read aloud this passage + record it back to the group","x":5840,"y":5360,"width":250,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"16b094a1f055ae75","type":"text","text":"rhy**th**m \nfreedom","x":5215,"y":12891,"width":250,"height":104},
		{"id":"6226ef8f7edc6dff","type":"text","text":"pre\\sent \n- noun: mon qua\n- verb: trinh bay - thuyet trinh ","x":5180,"y":13071,"width":290,"height":180},
		{"id":"61863a6ac69cc4be","type":"text","text":"CROSSCHECK","x":5520,"y":13161,"width":250,"height":58},
		{"id":"2219d4a76bacc0c8","type":"text","text":"HOMEWORK:\nCẢI THIỆN CÁC CÂU QUÁ \"DIRECT\" NÀY THÀNH CÁC CÂU REQUEST MANG TÍNH PHỐI HỢP \nDIRECT REQUEST -> COLLABORATIVE REQUEST","x":5840,"y":13251,"width":250,"height":195},
		{"id":"178e5bfc7295dbeb","type":"text","text":"**PPJ BUSINESS ENGLISH SPEAKING & LISTENING**\n\n**SESSION 7: FOLLOWING UP WITHOUT SOUNDING PUSHY**\n\nLevel: A1–A2  \n**Workplace theme: Pending responses and missing confirmations**  \nSpeaking outcome: Bạn có thể **hỏi tiến độ, nhắc lại yêu cầu** và **xin thời gian phản hồi** mà **không tạo cảm giác trách móc hoặc thúc ép**.\n\nTODAY I CAN\n\n□ I can follow up on a pending task politely.  \n□ I can ask for a clear status update.  \n□ I can explain why I need the information.  \n□ I can request a realistic response time.  \n□ I can agree on the next action.\n\n1. READING\n\n**A Professional Follow Up**\n\nThao works in the Import–Export Department. \nOn Monday morning, she asks a supplier to confirm the shipment date for PO 4582. \nThe supplier says they will send the confirmation *before Tuesday afternoon*.\n\nBy Wednesday morning, Thao still has no reply. \nThe Warehouse team needs the delivery information to ***prepare space for the goods.*** \nThe Production team also needs to ***update its work plan.***\n\nThao first wants to write:\n\n“Why haven’t you replied? Send the confirmation now.”\n\nHowever, **this message sounds angry and may create tension**. \nIt focuses on the supplier’s mistake, but it ***does not explain the business problem.***\n\nThao writes a new message:\n\n“Good morning, Mr. Lee. I’m following up on the shipment date con-fir-ma-tion for PO 4582. \nOur Warehouse and Production teams need the information to update their plans. \nCould you please let us ***know the current status*** by eleven thirty today? \nPlease let me know if you need any information from our side. \nThank you for your support.”\n\nThe supplier apologizes for the delay. \nThey are waiting for final approval from the carrier \nand promise to send an update before eleven thirty.\n\nThao’s message is polite, clear and specific. \nShe **focuses on moving the work forward instead of blaming the supplier.****\n\n**NEW VOCABULARY**\n\n| Word or phrase        | Meaning in Vietnamese              |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| follow up             | theo dõi và hỏi lại về một việc    |\n| confirmation          | sự xác nhận                        |\n| pending               | đang chờ xử lý                     |\n| current status        | trạng thái hiện tại                |\n| reminder              | lời nhắc                           |\n| delayed response      | phản hồi bị chậm                   |\n| carrier               | đơn vị vận chuyển                  |\n| final approval        | phê duyệt cuối cùng                |\n| create tension        | tạo ra sự căng thẳng               |\n| specific              | cụ thể                             |\n| response time         | thời gian phản hồi                 |\n| move the work forward | giúp công việc tiếp tục tiến triển |\n\n  \n  \n\n**MULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS**\n\n1. What is Thao waiting for?\n\nA. A payment report  \n**B. A shipment date confirmation**  \nC. A new invoice  \nD. A system update\n\n2. Which teams need the information?\n\nA. IT and Accounting  \n**B. Warehouse and Production**  \nC. HR and Purchasing  \nD. Finance and Inspection\n \n\n3. Why does Thao change her first message?\n\nA. It is too polite.  \nB. It has the wrong PO number.  \n**C. It sounds angry and does not explain the reason.**  \nD. It is too long.\n\n4. Why has the supplier not confirmed the shipment date?\n\nA. The invoice is incorrect.  \n**B. They are waiting for the carrier’s final approval.**  \nC. The warehouse is full.  \nD. Production changed the order.\n\n5. What makes Thao’s **second message** professional?\n\nA. She blames the supplier clearly.  \n**B. She explains the reason and asks for a response time.**  \nC. She sends the same message many times.  \nD. She removes all deadlines.  \n\n2. **TONE LADDER** \n\n**LEVEL 1: PUSHY OR BAD**\n\nThese sentences may sound blaming, impatient or demanding.\n\n- Why haven’t you replied yet?\n\n- Send me the confirmation now.\n\n- You promised to send it yesterday.\n\n- We have waited too long.\n\n*Why do they sound bad?*\n\n- They focus on the person’s failure.\n\n- They use commands.\n\n- They do not explain the **business reason**.\n\n- They may make the other person defensive.\n\n**LEVEL 2: POLITE**\n\n- ***Do you have any update*** on the **shipment date**?\n\n- ***Could you please check*** the current status?\n\n- **Could you let me know when** the confirmation will be available?\n\nThese sentences are respectful, but they are still clear.\n\n**LEVEL 3: COLLABORATIVE**\n\nI’m following up on the **shipment date** confirmation for **PO 4582**.\n\nOur Warehouse team needs the information to **prepare for the delivery**.\n\nCould you please update us by **eleven thirty today**?\n\nPlease let me know if **you need any information** from our side.\n\n**COLLABORATIVE FOLLOW UP FLOW**\n\n**Previous request**\n\n→ Current status\n\n→ Business reason\n\n→ Response time\n\n→ Offer support\n\n→ Polite closing\n\n**COMPLETE MODEL**\n\nGood morning, Mr. Lee. I’m following up on the shipment date confirmation for PO 4582. Our Warehouse team needs the information to prepare for the delivery. Could you please update us by eleven thirty today? Please let me know if you need any information from our side. Thank you for your support.\n\n3. EXPRESSION BANK\n\n**FUNCTION A: OPEN THE FOLLOW UP**\n\n| Complete expression                                    | Meaning in Vietnamese                       | Connected speech rhythm                     | PPJ workplace example                 | Rapid fire trigger        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| ***I’m following up on*** **my previous message.**     | Tôi đang theo dõi lại tin nhắn trước.       | I’m FOLlowing up / on my previous message.  | Supplier chưa phản hồi email hôm qua. | Theo dõi **tin nhắn cũ.** |\n| ***I’m following up on*** the **document request**.    | Tôi đang theo dõi **yêu cầu gửi chứng từ**. | I’m FOLlowing up / on the document request. | Packing list vẫn chưa được gửi.       | Nhắc **chứng từ.**        |\n| ***Just checking in on***  + Obj(the shipment update.) | Tôi đang hỏi lại về cập nhật lô hàng.       | Just CHECKing in / on the shipment update.  | Chưa nhận được ETA mới.               | Hỏi shipment.             |\n\n**FUNCTION B: ASK FOR THE CURRENT STATUS**\n\n| Complete expression                                  | Meaning in Vietnamese                                  | Connected speech rhythm                         | PPJ workplace example                  | Rapid fire trigger      |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| **Do you have any update on** + Object (this issue)? | Bạn có cập nhật gì về vấn đề này không?                | Do you have any UPdate / on this issue?         | Quantity mismatch vẫn chưa được xử lý. | Có update chưa?         |\n| **Could you update me on** the current status?       | Bạn có thể cập nhật trạng thái hiện tại cho tôi không? | Could you UPdate me / on the current status?    | Cần biết payment đang ở bước nào.      | Xin status.             |\n| Has the supplier confirmed the delivery date?        | Supplier đã xác nhận ngày giao hàng chưa?              | Has the supplier conFIRMED / the delivery date? | Warehouse đang chờ ngày nhận hàng.     | Supplier xác nhận chưa? |\n\n  \n\n**FUNCTION C: EXPLAIN THE BUSINESS REASON**\n\n| Complete expression                                            | Meaning in Vietnamese                                     | Connected speech rhythm                                        | PPJ workplace example             | Rapid fire trigger  |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| **We need the** confirmation **to** update our internal teams. | Chúng tôi cần xác nhận để cập nhật các team nội bộ.       | We need the confirMAtion / to update our internal teams.       | XNK cần cập nhật Kho và Sản xuất. | Nêu lý do nội bộ.   |\n| The warehouse is waiting for the delivery details.             | Kho đang chờ thông tin giao hàng.                         | The WAREhouse is waiting / for the delivery details.           | Kho cần chuẩn bị nhận hàng.       | Kho đang chờ.       |\n| We need this information to complete the shipment documents.   | Chúng tôi cần thông tin này để hoàn tất chứng từ lô hàng. | We need this inforMAtion / to complete the shipment documents. | Hồ sơ shipment chưa thể hoàn tất. | Cần hoàn tất hồ sơ. |\n\n**FUNCTION D: REQUEST A RESPONSE AND CLOSE**\n\n| Complete expression                                           | Meaning in Vietnamese                                     | Connected speech rhythm                                           | PPJ workplace example               | Rapid fire trigger   |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------- |\n| **Could you please update** us **by** noon today?             | Bạn có thể cập nhật trước trưa nay không?                 | Could you please UPdate us / by noon today?                       | Cần thông tin trước cuộc họp chiều. | Xin trước trưa.      |\n| When can we expect your confirmation?                         | Khi nào chúng tôi có thể nhận được xác nhận?              | When can we exPECT / your confirmation?                           | Supplier chưa cung cấp timeline.    | Khi nào có xác nhận? |\n| Please let me know if you need any information from our side. | Hãy cho tôi biết nếu bạn cần thông tin từ phía chúng tôi. | Please let me KNOW / if you need any information / from our side. | PPJ sẵn sàng bổ sung dữ liệu.       | Cần gì từ PPJ?       |\n\nRAPID FIRE PRACTICE\n\nBạn nghe trigger tiếng Việt và trả lời trong 5 giây.\n\n|Trigger|Complete response|\n|---|---|\n|Theo dõi tin nhắn cũ|I’m following up on my previous message.|\n|Nhắc chứng từ|I’m following up on the document request.|\n|Có update chưa?|Do you have any update on this issue?|\n|Xin status|Could you update me on the current status?|\n|Supplier xác nhận chưa?|Has the supplier confirmed the delivery date?|\n|Kho đang chờ|The warehouse is waiting for the delivery details.|\n|Cần hoàn tất hồ sơ|We need this information to complete the shipment documents.|\n|Xin trước trưa|Could you please update us by noon today?|\n|Khi nào có xác nhận?|When can we expect your confirmation?|\n|Cần gì từ PPJ?|Please let me know if you need any information from our side.|\n\n  \n\n4. THREE SPEAKING PATTERNS\n\nPATTERN 1: SIMPLE STATUS FOLLOW UP\n\nFramework\n\nI’m following up on + pending task.\n\n  \n\nDo you have any update on + specific information?\n\nSample answer\n\nI’m following up on the revised packing list. Do you have any update on the document status?\n\nYour answer\n\n|Part|Your information|\n|---|---|\n|Pending task||\n|Information you need||\n\nSay your complete follow up to your partner.\n\nPATTERN 2: FOLLOW UP WITH A REASON AND RESPONSE TIME\n\nFramework\n\nI’m following up on + pending task.\n\n  \n\nWe need the information to + business reason.\n\n  \n\nCould you please update us by + time?\n\nSample answer\n\nI’m following up on the shipment date confirmation. We need the information to update the Warehouse team. Could you please update us by noon today?\n\nYour answer\n\n|Part|Your information|\n|---|---|\n|Pending task||\n|Business reason||\n|Response time||\n\nSay your complete follow up twice.\n\nRound 1: Use your notes.\n\nRound 2: Speak without reading the full sentence.\n\nPATTERN 3: COMPLETE COLLABORATIVE FOLLOW UP\n\nFramework\n\nGood morning, + name.\n\n  \n\nI’m following up on + pending task.\n\n  \n\nWe need it because + business reason.\n\n  \n\nWhen can we expect + required information?\n\n  \n\nPlease let me know if you need + support or information.\n\n  \n\nThank you for your support.\n\nSample answer\n\nGood morning, Mr. Lee. I’m following up on the delivery date confirmation for PO 4582. We need it because Warehouse is preparing to receive the goods. When can we expect the final confirmation? Please let me know if you need any information from our side. Thank you for your support.\n\nYour answer\n\n|Part|Your information|\n|---|---|\n|Person’s name||\n|Pending task||\n|Business reason||\n|Information you need||\n|Support you can offer||\n\nGive your complete message to a partner.\n\nYour partner must answer:\n\nWe are still working on it.\n\nContinue the conversation and ask for a response time.\n\n5. **TRANSFORM THE SENTENCES**\n\nChange each pushy, unclear or incomplete sentence into a polite and collaborative follow up.\n\n| Pushy or unclear sentence              | Your professional version                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Send me the confirmation now.          | I'm following up on + the confirmation that we talked about last week. Do you have any update on it? Please let me know if you need any additional information. |\n| Why are you not replying?              |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Any update?                            |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| We are still waiting.                  |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| You promised to send it yesterday.     |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Tell me when the shipment will arrive. |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Reply before lunch.                    |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| The warehouse needs this now.          |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Check the payment status again.        |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| This is urgent. Do it immediately.     |                                                                                                                                                                 |\n\nUSE THIS CHECKLIST\n\nA strong transformation should include at least three elements.\n\n□ What you are following up on  \n□ Why the information is needed  \n□ When you need the response  \n□ A polite question  \n□ An offer of support  \n□ A professional closing\n\nMODEL TRANSFORMATION\n\nPushy\n\nWhy haven’t you sent the file?\n\nCollaborative\n\nI’m following up on the file request from yesterday. We need the file to complete the shipment documents. Could you please let me know when it will be available?\n\n6. ROLEPLAY: MISSING SUPPLIER CONFIRMATION\n\nSITUATION\n\nPPJ is waiting for a supplier to confirm the shipment date for PO 4582.\n\n|Information|Details|\n|---|---|\n|Expected confirmation|Tuesday afternoon|\n|Current time|Wednesday at 9:30 a.m.|\n|Warehouse deadline|Before noon|\n|Internal impact|Production also needs the shipment date|\n\n  \n  \n\nROLE A: PPJ IMPORT EXPORT\n\nYou need to:\n\n1. Mention the previous request.\n    \n2. Ask for the current status.\n    \n3. Explain why PPJ needs the information.\n    \n4. Ask for a clear response time.\n    \n5. Offer support.\n    \n6. Close politely.\n    \n\nUse at least five sentences.\n\nI’m following up on my previous message.\n\n  \n\nDo you have any update on the shipment date?\n\n  \n\nThe warehouse is waiting for the delivery details.\n\n  \n\nCould you please update us by noon today?\n\n  \n\nWhen can we expect your confirmation?\n\n  \n\nPlease let me know if you need any information from our side.\n\n  \n\nThank you for your support.\n\n  \n  \n\nROLE B: SUPPLIER\n\nYour situation:\n\n|Information|Details|\n|---|---|\n|Current problem|The carrier has not given final approval.|\n|Expected carrier response|11:00 a.m.|\n|Your update to PPJ|11:30 a.m.|\n|Information you need|Confirmation of the delivery address|\n\nUse at least four sentences.\n\nI’m sorry for the delayed response.\n\n  \n\nWe’re still waiting for final approval from the carrier.\n\n  \n\nWe expect an update at eleven o’clock.\n\n  \n\nI can send you the confirmation by eleven thirty.\n\n  \n\nCould you confirm the delivery address?\n\n  \n\nThank you for your patience.  \n\nCONVERSATION FLOW\n\nGreeting\n\n→ Previous request\n\n→ Current status question\n\n→ Reason for the delay\n\n→ Business impact\n\n→ Response time → Information needed → Next action → Polite closing\n\nFINAL AGREEMENT\n\nComplete the summary together.\n\n|Item|Agreed information|\n|---|---|\n|The supplier is waiting for||\n|The supplier will update PPJ by||\n|PPJ will send||\n|Warehouse and Production will be updated after||\n\nSUCCESS CHECK\n\n□ I mentioned the previous request.  \n□ I asked for a clear update.  \n□ I explained why the information was needed.  \n□ I asked for a realistic response time.  \n□ I avoided blaming language.  \n□ I offered support or information.  \n□ We agreed on the next action.  \n□ I closed politely.  \n\n7. SESSION TAKEAWAY\n\nA professional follow up does not focus on:\n\nWhy haven’t you replied?\n\nIt focuses on:\n\nWhat is pending?\n\n+\n\nWhy is the information needed?\n\n+\n\nWhen is the update required?\n\n+\n\nWhat is the next action?\n\nFIVE SENTENCES TO REMEMBER\n\nI’m following up on my previous message.\n\nDo you have any update on this issue?\n\nWe need the information to update our internal teams.\n\nCould you please update us by noon today?\n\nPlease let me know if you need any information from our side.  \n\nFINAL MESSAGE\n\nFollow up on the work without attacking the person.\n\nNội dung chủ đề và đầu ra được phát triển theo Session 7 trong course master plan.\n\n  \n**","x":9080,"y":10800,"width":920,"height":18243},
		{"id":"1068ec55f2d21ba8","type":"text","text":"# STUDENT WORKSHEET\n\n## TENSES FOR REAL WORKPLACE COMMUNICATION\n\nLevel: A2–B1  \nClass time: 75 minutes + 15 minutes Kahoot  \nFocus: Use tenses to talk about routines, current situations, past events, experience, ongoing past actions, and future plans.\n\n### Learning Goals\n\nBy the end of this lesson, you can:\n\n- describe what you usually do\n    \n- explain what is happening now\n    \n- report what happened\n    \n- talk about an action that was happening\n    \n- explain what has happened / has changed\n    \n- talk about future plans, decisions, and predictions\n    \n\n## 1. THE BIG PICTURE: 6 TENSES YOU REALLY NEED\n\n|   |   |   |   |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Tense|Main Idea|Common Time Markers|Workplace Example|\n|Present Simple|routine / fact|usually, every day, often, normally|I check invoices every morning.|\n|Present Continuous|happening now / temporary|now, right now, currently, this week|I’m checking a supplier invoice now.|\n|Past Simple|finished past event|yesterday, last week, this morning|We received the documents yesterday.|\n|Past Continuous|action in progress in the past|while, when, at 3 p.m. yesterday|I was checking the report when she called.|\n|Present Perfect|past + connection to now|already, yet, just, ever, never, since, for|We have received the revised file.|\n|Future|plan / decision / prediction|tomorrow, next week, later|I’ll contact the supplier later.|\n\n### The Core Question\n\nBefore choosing a tense, ask:\n\nWhat TIME am I talking about, and how is the action connected to that time?\n\n## 2. READING: ONE BUSY DAY AT WORK\n\nRead the story. Underline the verbs.\n\n### A Busy Morning\n\nLinh works in the Purchasing Department. She usually checks supplier confirmations before 9 a.m.\n\nToday is different. She is dealing with an urgent material issue because Production needs the fabric tomorrow.\n\nYesterday, the supplier sent a confirmation, but the quantity was incorrect. Linh was reviewing another purchase order when the warehouse called her about the problem.\n\nShe has already contacted the supplier and has received a revised confirmation. However, the supplier has not confirmed the delivery time yet.\n\nLinh says:\n\n“I’ll follow up with them again this afternoon. We’re going to update Production as soon as we receive the final confirmation.”\n\n  \n  \n\n### Check Your Understanding\n\nChoose the best answer.\n\n1. What does Linh normally do before 9 a.m.?\n\nA. Contact Production  \nB. Check supplier confirmations  \nC. Receive materials  \nD. Prepare invoices\n\n2. Why is today different?\n\nA. She is on leave.  \nB. The warehouse is closed.  \nC. She is handling an urgent material issue.  \nD. The supplier cancelled the order.\n\n3. What happened yesterday?\n\nA. The supplier sent an incorrect confirmation.  \nB. Production changed the order.  \nC. Linh received the fabric.  \nD. The warehouse rejected the materials.\n\n4. What was Linh doing when the warehouse called?\n\nA. Contacting the supplier  \nB. Reviewing another PO  \nC. Updating Production  \nD. Checking an invoice\n\n5. What has Linh already done?\n\nA. Received the materials  \nB. Cancelled the PO  \nC. Contacted the supplier  \nD. Confirmed the delivery time\n\n6. What will she do later?\n\nA. Follow up with the supplier  \nB. Create another PO  \nC. Visit the warehouse  \nD. Cancel the shipment\n\n## 3. TENSE 1: PRESENT SIMPLE\n\n### Use it for\n\nRoutine\n\nI check the stock every morning.\n\nRegular responsibility\n\nFinance prepares the monthly report.\n\nFact\n\nOur warehouse stores finished goods.\n\n### Pattern\n\nI / You / We / They + verb\n\nWe check the data.\n\nHe / She / It + verb-s\n\nShe checks the data.\n\n### Workplace Triggers\n\n- every day\n    \n- usually\n    \n- normally\n    \n- often\n    \n- sometimes\n    \n- always\n    \n- once a week\n    \n\n### Your Turn\n\nComplete the sentences.\n\n1. I usually __________ before I start work.\n    \n2. My department normally __________.\n    \n3. We often work with __________.\n    \n4. I sometimes need English when __________.\n    \n\n## 4. TENSE 2: PRESENT CONTINUOUS\n\n### Use it for\n\nSomething happening now\n\nI’m checking the invoice right now.\n\nA temporary situation\n\nWe’re working on a new project this month.\n\n### Pattern\n\nam / is / are + verb-ing\n\nI’m checking it.\n\nShe’s talking to the supplier.\n\nThey’re preparing the shipment.\n\n### Compare\n\nRoutine\n\nI check invoices every morning.\n\nRight now\n\nI’m checking an invoice now.\n\n### Your Turn\n\nWhat is happening in your department right now / this week?\n\n5. I’m currently ______________________________.\n    \n6. My team is _________________________________.\n    \n7. We’re working on ___________________________.\n    \n\n## 5. TENSE 3: PAST SIMPLE\n\n### Use it for\n\nA finished action in the past.\n\nThe supplier sent the document yesterday.\n\nWe found an error this morning.\n\nProduction changed the quantity last week.\n\n### Common Signals\n\n- yesterday\n    \n- last week\n    \n- two days ago\n    \n- this morning\n    \n- in July\n    \n- at 10 a.m.\n    \n\n### Regular vs Irregular\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Present|Past|\n|check|checked|\n|receive|received|\n|contact|contacted|\n|send|sent|\n|find|found|\n|make|made|\n|have|had|\n|go|went|\n\n### Complete Your Story\n\nThink about one problem you handled recently.\n\nYesterday / Last week, __________________________________.\n\nThe problem was ________________________________________.\n\nI contacted _____________________________________________.\n\nWe decided to ___________________________________________.\n\nFinally, ________________________________________________.\n\n## 6. TENSE 4: PAST CONTINUOUS\n\n### Use it for\n\nAn action that was already happening when another event occurred.\n\nI was checking the report when my manager called.\n\n### Pattern\n\nwas / were + verb-ing\n\n### Useful Speaking Pattern\n\nI was ___ing when ___ happened.\n\nExamples:\n\nI was preparing the report when the system stopped working.\n\nWe were discussing the shipment when the supplier called.\n\n### Your Turn\n\nComplete naturally.\n\n1. I was working on __________ when __________.\n    \n2. We were checking __________ when __________.\n    \n3. The team was discussing __________ when __________.\n    \n\n## 7. TENSE 5: PRESENT PERFECT\n\nThis is one of the most useful tenses in workplace English.\n\n### Use it when\n\nSomething happened before and the result matters NOW.\n\nWe have received the document.\n\nMeaning:\n\nThe document is available now.\n\n### Pattern\n\nhave / has + past participle\n\nI have sent it.\n\nShe has checked it.\n\nThey have finished the report.\n\n### High-Frequency Workplace Expressions\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Expression|Meaning|\n|I’ve sent it.|Tôi gửi rồi.|\n|We’ve received it.|Bên tôi nhận được rồi.|\n|I’ve already checked it.|Tôi kiểm tra rồi.|\n|We haven’t received it yet.|Bên tôi vẫn chưa nhận được.|\n|Has the supplier confirmed it yet?|NCC xác nhận chưa?|\n|There has been a change.|Đã có thay đổi.|\n|We’ve found an issue.|Bên tôi phát hiện một vấn đề.|\n\n### Past Simple vs Present Perfect\n\nPast Simple = WHEN matters\n\nI sent it yesterday.\n\nPresent Perfect = RESULT NOW matters\n\nI’ve sent it.\n\nCompare:\n\nDid you send the report yesterday?\n\nHave you sent the report yet?\n\n## 8. TENSE 6: TALKING ABOUT THE FUTURE\n\n### WILL\n\nUse for:\n\nDecision now\n\nI’ll check it.\n\nPromise\n\nI’ll send you an update.\n\nPrediction\n\nI think the shipment will arrive tomorrow.\n\n### BE GOING TO\n\nUse for an existing intention or plan.\n\nWe’re going to review the report tomorrow.\n\n### PRESENT CONTINUOUS FOR ARRANGEMENTS\n\nUse when something is already arranged.\n\nI’m meeting the supplier at 2 p.m.\n\n### Compare\n\nSituation:\n\nYour colleague asks:\n\n“Can you check this file?”\n\nYou decide now:\n\nSure, I’ll check it.\n\nYou already planned it:\n\nI’m going to check it this afternoon.\n\nYou already have a scheduled review:\n\nI’m reviewing it with Finance at 3 p.m.\n\n## 9. CHOOSE THE TENSE\n\nChoose the best answer.\n\n### 1\n\nI usually _____ the inventory report every Monday.\n\n**A. prepare**  \nB. am preparing  \nC. prepared  \nD. have prepared\n\n### 2\n\nPlease give me five minutes. I am checking_____ the information **now.**\n\nA. check  \nB. checked  \nC. am checking  \nD. have checked\n\n### 3\n\nThe supplier sent the revised invoice yesterday.\n\nA. sends  \n**B. sent**  \nC. has sent  \nD. is sending\n\n### 4\n\nI _____ the report when **my manager called me.** \n\n**A. had prepared** - da hoan tat truoc khi manager called me  \nB. have prepared  \n**C. was preparing**  - muon nhan manh viec dang chuan bi trong khi manager called me\nD. prepare\n\n### 5\n\nWe _____ the documents **yet** ///// **yet + perfect**\n\nA. didn't receive  \n**B. haven't received**  \nC. don't receive  \nD. aren't receiving\n\n### 6\n\nDon’t worry. I _____ the warehouse.\n\nA. contact  \nB. contacted  \n**C. have contacted**  --- nhan manh vao viec khong phai lo - **vi moi thu da em xuoi, hoan thanh roi**\n**D. will contact** --- nhan manh vao viec khong phai lo - **vi toi se handle viec do**\n\n  \n  \n\n### 7\n\nShe _____ in Purchasing **for three years**. /////\n- *for + time* --> perfect: **she has worked in PUR for 3 years**\n- *since + time* --> perfect: **she has worked in PUR since 2022**\n\nA. works  \nB. worked  \n**C. has worked**  \nD. is working yesterday\n\n### 8\n\nWe _____ with Finance at 3 p.m. tomorrow. The meeting is already scheduled.\n\nA. met  \n**B. \nare meeting**  - 100%  \nbe going to -> 6-70%\nwill -> 50%\nC. meet yesterday  \nD. have met\n\n## 10. TENSE TRANSFORMATION\n\nChange the sentence according to the situation.\n\n### Example\n\n**Routine:**  \nI check supplier confirmations.\n\n**Now:**  \n*I’m checking* a supplier confirmation.\n\n### A\n\n**Routine**\n\nWe check the inventory every morning.\n\n**Right now**\n\n  \n\n### B\n\nNow\n\nI’m discussing the issue with Production.\n\nYesterday\n\n  \n\n### C\n\nFinished yesterday\n\nThe supplier sent the invoice yesterday.\n\nResult matters now\n\n  \n\n### D\n\nAction in progress\n\nI was reviewing the PO.\n\nAdd interruption:\n\n__________________________________ when __________.\n\n### E\n\nProblem now\n\nWe haven’t received the document yet.\n\nMake a future action:\n\n  \n\n## 11. THREE SPEAKING PATTERNS\n\n### Pattern 1: ROUTINE → CURRENT SITUATION\n\nNormally, I __________, but today I’m __________.\n\nExample:\n\nNormally, I prepare regular reports, but today I’m working on an urgent request.\n\nYour sentence:\n\nNormally, I ____________________, but today ____________________.\n\n### Pattern 2: PAST EVENT → CURRENT RESULT\n\nYesterday, __________. So now, we’ve __________.\n\nExample:\n\nYesterday, we found a quantity mismatch. So now, we’ve asked the supplier to revise the document.\n\nYour sentence:\n\nYesterday, ____________________. So now, ____________________.\n\n### Pattern 3: PROBLEM → FUTURE ACTION\n\nWe haven’t __________ yet, so I’ll __________.\n\nExample:\n\nWe haven’t received confirmation yet, so I’ll follow up this afternoon.\n\nYour sentence:\n\nWe haven’t ____________________, so I’ll ____________________.\n\n  \n  \n  \n\n## 12. RAPID-FIRE TENSE CHALLENGE\n\nYour partner gives you a time trigger. Say one workplace sentence immediately.\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Trigger|Use|\n|Every Monday|Present Simple|\n|Right now|Present Continuous|\n|Yesterday|Past Simple|\n|When my manager called|Past Continuous|\n|Already|Present Perfect|\n|Yet|Present Perfect|\n|Tomorrow|Future|\n|Next week|Future|\n|For three years|Present Perfect|\n|Last year|Past Simple|\n\n### Example\n\nPartner: “Right now!”\n\nYou:\n\nI’m checking the monthly report right now.\n\n## 13. FIND AND FIX THE MISTAKE\n\nCorrect each sentence.\n\n4. I am usually check the report every morning.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n5. Yesterday I have contacted the supplier.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n6. I working on the invoice now.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n7. We haven't received the documents yesterday.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n8. I was check the PO when she called.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n9. The supplier hasn't reply yet.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n10. Tomorrow I contacted the warehouse.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n11. She work here for five years.  \n    → ___________________________________________\n    \n\n  \n  \n  \n\n## 14. PAIR ROLEPLAY: THE MISSING MATERIAL CONFIRMATION\n\n### Situation\n\nProduction needs material urgently.\n\nThe supplier sent some information yesterday, but the final delivery confirmation has not arrived.\n\n### Student A: Purchasing\n\nExplain:\n\n- what you normally do\n    \n- what happened yesterday\n    \n- what you are doing now\n    \n- what you have already done\n    \n- what has not happened yet\n    \n- what you will do next\n    \n\n### Student B: Production\n\nAsk:\n\n- What happened?\n    \n- When did you contact the supplier?\n    \n- Have they replied yet?\n    \n- What are you doing now?\n    \n- What will you do next?\n    \n- When can Production expect an update?\n    \n\n### Useful Expressions\n\nWe usually…\n\nYesterday, we…\n\nI was … when…\n\nWe’ve already…\n\nWe haven’t … yet.\n\nI’m currently…\n\nI’ll…\n\nWe’re going to…\n\n### Challenge\n\nUse at least five different tenses/forms during the conversation.\n\n  \n  \n\n## 15. SPEAKING: MY WORK TIMELINE\n\nTalk to a partner.\n\n### Routine\n\nWhat do you normally do at work?\n\nI usually…\n\n### Now\n\nWhat are you currently working on?\n\nRight now, I’m…\n\n### Recent Past\n\nWhat did you do yesterday?\n\nYesterday, I…\n\n### Interrupted Action\n\nWhat were you doing when someone contacted you recently?\n\nI was… when…\n\n### Recent Result\n\nWhat have you completed recently?\n\nI’ve already…\n\n### Unfinished Task\n\nWhat haven’t you finished yet?\n\nI haven’t… yet.\n\n### Future\n\nWhat will you do after class / tomorrow?\n\nI’ll…\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n## 16. FINAL CHALLENGE: TELL ONE COMPLETE WORK STORY\n\nSpeak for 60–90 seconds.\n\nYour story must include:\n\n1. Present Simple — your normal responsibility\n    \n2. Present Continuous — what is happening now\n    \n3. Past Simple — what happened\n    \n4. Past Continuous — what was happening\n    \n5. Present Perfect — current result\n    \n6. Future — next action\n    \n\n### Story Frame\n\nNormally, I __________________________.\n\nToday, I’m __________________________.\n\nYesterday, __________________________.\n\nI was __________________ when __________________.\n\nWe’ve already _______________________.\n\nHowever, we haven’t __________________ yet.\n\nNext, I’ll ___________________________.\n\n## TAKEAWAY\n\nDon't ask:\n\n“Which tense should I use?”\n\nAsk:\n\n“What time am I talking about?”\n\n### Remember\n\nRoutine → Present Simple  \nNow → Present Continuous  \nFinished past → Past Simple  \nIn progress in the past → Past Continuous  \nPast + result now → Present Perfect  \nNext action / plan → Future\n\nThe goal is not to memorize 12 tense formulas.\n\nThe goal is to move naturally between past → present → future when telling a real story.\n\n  \n**","x":10752,"y":9183,"width":788,"height":23234},
		{"id":"d4d9a80491192d29","type":"text","text":"homework 3: hoan thanh transformation of sentences","x":8900,"y":18060,"width":173,"height":120},
		{"id":"412de5ac4aebd360","type":"text","text":"## Phân biệt Simple Past và Present Perfect\n\n### 1. Simple Past = việc đã kết thúc trong quá khứ\n\n**Cấu trúc:**\n\n> S + V2/V-ed\n\nDùng khi **thời điểm trong quá khứ đã rõ hoặc đã kết thúc**.\n\n**Ví dụ:**\n\n- I **sent** the email yesterday.\n    \n- She **worked** at PPJ in 2024.\n    \n- We **met** the supplier last Monday.\n    \n- I **visited** Thailand three years ago.\n    \n\nTừ khóa thường gặp:\n\n- yesterday\n    \n- last week / last year\n    \n- two days ago\n    \n- in 2025\n    \n- when I was younger\n    \n\n### 2. Present Perfect = quá khứ có liên hệ với hiện tại\n\n**Cấu trúc:**\n\n> S + have/has + V3\n\nKhông tập trung vào **khi nào**, mà tập trung vào **kết quả, trải nghiệm hoặc khoảng thời gian kéo dài đến hiện tại**.\n\n**Ví dụ:**\n\n- I **have sent** the email.  \n    → Email đã được gửi rồi, **đó là tình trạng hiện tại**.\n    \n- She **has worked** at PPJ for five years.  \n    → Cô ấy bắt đầu 5 năm trước và **vẫn đang làm ở PPJ**.\n    - she hás worked at PPJ **since** 2024\n    \n- We **have met** this supplier several times.  \n    → Đây là trải nghiệm tính đến hiện tại.\n    \n- I **have visited** Thailand three times.  \n    → Không quan trọng chính xác khi nào.\n    \n\n### 3. So sánh trực tiếp\n\n|Simple Past|Present Perfect|\n|---|---|\n|Quá khứ đã kết thúc|Quá khứ liên quan đến hiện tại|\n|Có thời điểm quá khứ rõ|Thường không nói thời điểm cụ thể|\n|**When did it happen?**|**Has it happened yet / ever?**|\n|V2|have/has + V3|\n\nVí dụ rất quan trọng:\n\n**I worked at PPJ for five years.**  \n→ Tôi đã làm PPJ 5 năm, **nhưng bây giờ không còn làm nữa**.\n\n**I have worked at PPJ for five years.**  \n→ Tôi đã làm PPJ được 5 năm và **hiện vẫn đang làm**.\n\n### 4. Một cặp câu rất dễ nhầm\n\n**Did you send the invoice yesterday?**  \n→ Hỏi về **yesterday**, nên Simple Past.\n\n**Have you sent the invoice yet?**  \n→ Hỏi xem **đến hiện tại đã gửi chưa**, nên Present Perfect.\n\nTương tự:\n\n- When **did you receive** the document?\n    \n- **Have you received** the document yet?\n    \n\n### 5. Mẹo nhớ nhanh\n\nHãy tự hỏi:\n\n> **Có nói rõ WHEN trong một khoảng thời gian đã kết thúc không?**\n\nCó → **Simple Past**\n\n> I called him **this morning**.  \n> _(nếu buổi sáng đã kết thúc)_\n\nKhông, chỉ quan tâm **đến hiện tại đã xảy ra chưa / bao nhiêu lần / kéo dài bao lâu** → **Present Perfect**\n\n> I have called him three times / today.\n\n### 6. Những từ thường đi với Present Perfect\n\n- already\n    \n- yet\n    \n- just\n    \n- ever // have you ever + ....\n    \n- never\n    \n- recently\n    \n- so far\n    \n- for + time\n    \n- since + time in the past\n    \n- several times\n    \n\nVí dụ:\n\n- I’ve **already checked** the report.\n    \n- Have you **finished yet**?\n    \n- We’ve **just received** the confirmation.\n    \n- I’ve **never worked** with this supplier before.\n    \n- She has worked here **since 2022**.\n    \n- She has worked here **for four years**.\n    \n\n### Reflex cần nhớ\n\n> **Past Simple = WHEN?**  \n> **Present Perfect = UP TO NOW?**\n\nVí dụ workplace:\n\n**When did the supplier reply?**  \n→ Yesterday. → Past Simple\n\n**Has the supplier replied yet?**  \n→ Yes, they have. → Present Perfect","x":11920,"y":5800,"width":720,"height":2960},
		{"id":"9cce903663d539c4","type":"text","text":"# Bài tập: Present Simple → Past Simple → Present Perfect\n\n### Cách làm\n\nMỗi câu ban đầu ở **Present Simple**. Viết lại thành:\n\n1. **Past Simple** theo ngữ cảnh quá khứ đã kết thúc.\n    \n2. **Present Perfect** theo ngữ cảnh có liên hệ đến hiện tại.\n    \n\n### Example\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nI check the invoice every morning.\n\n**Past context:** yesterday morning  \n→ I **checked the invoice yesterday morning**.\n\n**Present Perfect context:** already / today  \n→ I **have already checked the invoice today**.\n\n## Exercise\n\n### 1\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nI send reports to my manager every Friday.\n\n**Past context:** last Friday  \n→ ____________________________________________Last friday, i sent reports to my manager.\n\n**Present Perfect context:** already / this week  \n→ ____________________________________________i have already sent reports to my manager this week\n\n### 2\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nShe checks the supplier documents carefully.\n\n**Past context:** yesterday  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** all the documents / already  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 3\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nWe receive many requests from the warehouse.\n\n**Past context:** yesterday morning  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** three requests / so far today  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 4\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nHe works with the Purchasing Department.\n\n**Past context:** in 2024  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** for two years / still works there  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 5\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nThey meet the supplier every month.\n\n**Past context:** last Monday  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** twice / this month  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 6\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nI finish my tasks before 5 p.m.\n\n**Past context:** yesterday  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** all my tasks / already  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 7\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nThe supplier sends us the packing list.\n\n**Past context:** two days ago  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** just  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 8\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nWe find mistakes in the invoice sometimes.\n\n**Past context:** during yesterday's check  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** two mistakes / so far  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 9\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nShe is responsible for this report.\n\n**Past context:** last year  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** since January  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n### 10\n\n**Present Simple:**  \nI talk to the production team about this problem.\n\n**Past context:** this morning  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n**Present Perfect context:** several times / this week  \n→ ____________________________________________\n\n# Answer Key\n\n|#|Past Simple|Present Perfect|\n|---|---|---|\n|1|I **sent** the report to my manager last Friday.|I **have already sent** the report this week.|\n|2|She **checked** the supplier documents yesterday.|She **has already checked** all the documents.|\n|3|We **received** many requests from the warehouse yesterday morning.|We **have received** three requests so far today.|\n|4|He **worked** with the Purchasing Department in 2024.|He **has worked** with the Purchasing Department for two years.|\n|5|They **met** the supplier last Monday.|They **have met** the supplier twice this month.|\n|6|I **finished** my tasks yesterday.|I **have already finished** all my tasks.|\n|7|The supplier **sent** us the packing list two days ago.|The supplier **has just sent** us the packing list.|\n|8|We **found** mistakes in the invoice during yesterday's check.|We **have found** two mistakes so far.|\n|9|She **was** responsible for this report last year.|She **has been** responsible for this report since January.|\n|10|I **talked** to the production team about this problem this morning.|I **have talked** to the production team about this problem several times this week.|\n\n## Pattern học viên cần nhận ra\n\n> **Present Simple:** What usually happens?  \n> I check invoices every day.\n\n> **Past Simple:** What happened at a finished time?  \n> I checked the invoice **yesterday**.\n\n> **Present Perfect:** What has happened up to now?  \n> I have checked three invoices **so far today**.\n\nĐặc biệt câu 9 rất đáng luyện:\n\n> She **is** responsible. → Present Simple  \n> She **was** responsible. → Past Simple  \n> She **has been** responsible. → Present Perfect\n\nĐây cũng là cách rất tốt để học viên luyện luôn chuỗi **is → was → has been**.","x":13280,"y":5480,"width":737,"height":4080},
		{"id":"d37f362703de9611","type":"text","text":"\n## 8. TENSE 6: TALKING ABOUT THE FUTURE\n\n### WILL\n\nUse for:\n\n**Decision now**\n\nI’ll check it.\n\n**Promise**\n\nI’ll send you an update.\n\n**Prediction**\n\nI think the shipment will arrive tomorrow.\n\n### BE GOING TO\n\nUse for an **existing intention or plan.**\n\nWe’re going to **review the report** tomorrow.\n\n### PRESENT CONTINUOUS FOR ARRANGEMENTS -- 90-95%\n\n**Use when something is already arranged.**\n\nI’m meeting the supplier at 2 p.m.\n\n### Compare\n\nSituation:\n\nYour colleague asks:\n\n“Can you check this file?”\n\nYou decide now:\n\nSure, I’ll check it.\n\nYou already planned it:\n\nI’m going to check it this afternoon.\n\nYou already have a scheduled review:\n\nI’m reviewing it with Finance at 3 p.m.\n\n**","x":12080,"y":17280,"width":650,"height":1100},
		{"id":"d3d7263fb12a8b93","type":"text","text":"**PPJ BUSINESS ENGLISH SPEAKING & LISTENING\n\nSESSION 8: EXPLAINING A WORK PROBLEM CLEARLY\n\nLevel: A1–A2  \nWorkplace theme: Problems, causes, impact and next actions  \nSpeaking outcome: Bạn có thể giải thích một vấn đề công việc theo trình tự rõ ràng, không đổ lỗi và đề xuất bước xử lý tiếp theo.\n\nTODAY I CAN\n\n□ I can state the main problem clearly.  \n□ I can explain what caused the problem.  \n□ I can describe how the problem affects the work.  \n□ I can give the current status.  \n□ I can suggest a clear next action.  \n□ I can give a short issue update without blaming anyone.\n\n1. READING\n\nA Clear Problem Report\n\nMinh works in the Warehouse Department. On Wednesday morning, his team receives a delivery from a supplier. According to the packing list, the shipment should contain 500 pieces. However, the warehouse team only counts 480 pieces.\n\nMinh first wants to tell Purchasing team\n\n“The supplier made a mistake. The shipment is wrong.”\n\nHowever, this message does not give enough information. It also sounds like Minh is blaming the supplier before the team checks all the documents.\n\nMinh gives a clearer update:\n\n“We found a quantity difference in today’s delivery. The packing list shows 500 pieces, but we received 480 pieces. We may be missing 20 pieces. As a result, we cannot complete the receiving process yet. We are currently checking the cartons and cross-checking the delivery documents. Could Import–Export contact the supplier and confirm the shipped quantity?”\n\nPurchasing team understands the problem and contacts the supplier. The supplier checks the records and says that one carton was not loaded onto the truck. They agree to send the missing carton the next day.\n\nA clear problem report should explain the \n- problem, \n- cause, \n- impact, \n- current status \n- and next action. \n\n**It should focus on facts and solutions instead of blame.**\n\nNEW VOCABULARY\n\n|Word or phrase|Meaning in Vietnamese|\n|---|---|\n|issue|vấn đề cần xử lý|\n|quantity difference|chênh lệch số lượng|\n|according to|theo như, căn cứ theo|\n|receive|nhận hàng|\n|missing|bị thiếu|\n|cause|nguyên nhân|\n|impact|ảnh hưởng|\n|current status|trạng thái hiện tại|\n|cross-check|kiểm tra chéo|\n|receiving process|quy trình nhận hàng|\n|take action|thực hiện hành động|\n|blame|đổ lỗi|\n|shipment record|hồ sơ lô hàng|\n|next step|bước tiếp theo|\n\nMULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS\n\n1. How many pieces are shown on the packing list?\n\nA. 420 pieces  \nB. 480 pieces  \n**C. 500 pieces**  \nD. 520 pieces\n\n2. How many pieces does the warehouse receive?\n\nA. 450 pieces  \n**B. 480 pieces**  \nC. 500 pieces  \nD. 580 pieces\n\n3. Why does Minh change his first message?\n\nA. It is too polite.  \nB. It is too long.  \n**C. It does not give enough information and sounds blaming.**  \nD. It contains the wrong supplier name.\n\n4. What is the warehouse team doing now?\n\nA. Preparing the payment  \n**B. Checking the cartons and delivery documents**  \nC. Sending the goods back  \nD. Updating the invoice amount\n\n5. What is the main lesson of the reading?\n\n**A. A good report should focus on facts and solutions.**  \nB. The supplier should always be blamed first.  \nC. Every problem should be reported in one sentence.  \nD. The warehouse should solve every issue alone.\n\n2. TONE LADDER\n\n**LEVEL 1: BAD, UNCLEAR OR BLAMING**\n\nThe supplier made a mistake.\n\nThe shipment is wrong.\n\nWarehouse did not check the goods properly.\n\nThis problem is not our responsibility.\n\nThese statements may create tension because they:\n\n1. blame a person or department;\n    \n2. do not give clear facts;\n    \n3. do not explain the impact;\n    \n4. do not suggest a solution.\n    \n\n**LEVEL 2: POLITE AND FACTUAL**\n\nThere is a quantity difference in today’s delivery.\n\nThe packing list shows 500 pieces, but we received 480 pieces.\n\nWe are currently checking the cartons and documents.\n\nThese statements describe the facts without attacking anyone.\n\n**LEVEL 3: COLLABORATIVE AND SOLUTION FOCUSED**\n\nWe found a quantity difference in today’s delivery.\n\nAs a result, we cannot complete the receiving process yet.\n\nWe are checking the cartons and cross-checking the documents.\n\nCould Import–Export *contact the supplier and confirm the shipped quantity*?\n\n**CLEAR PROBLEM REPORT FLOW**\n\nProblem\n\n→ Cause\n\n→ Impact\n\n→ Current status\n\n→ Next action\n\nCOMPLETE MODEL\n\nWe found a quantity difference in today’s delivery. The packing list shows 500 pieces, but Warehouse received 480 pieces. The issue may be related to one missing carton. As a result, we cannot complete the receiving process yet. We are currently checking the cartons and delivery documents. Could Import–Export contact the supplier and confirm the shipped quantity?\n\n3. EXPRESSION BANK\n\nFUNCTION A: STATE THE PROBLEM\n\n| Complete expression                                          | Meaning in Vietnamese                                          | Connected speech rhythm                                     | PPJ workplace example                    | Rapid fire trigger        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| We found a **quantity difference** in today’s delivery.      | Chúng tôi phát hiện chênh lệch số lượng trong lô hàng hôm nay. | We found / a QUANtity difference / in today’s delivery.     | Packing list ghi 500 nhưng Kho nhận 480. | Có chênh lệch số lượng.   |\n| There seems to be an **issue with the shipment documents**.  | Có vẻ đang có vấn đề với chứng từ lô hàng.                     | There seems to be / an ISSUE / with the shipment documents. | Packing list và invoice không khớp.      | Chứng từ có vấn đề.       |\n| The information in **the system does not match the report.** | Thông tin trên hệ thống không khớp với báo cáo.                | The information / in the SYStem / doesn’t match the report. | WFX hiển thị quantity khác file báo cáo. | System không khớp report. |\n\nFUNCTION B: EXPLAIN THE CAUSE\n\n| Complete expression                                         | Meaning in Vietnamese                                               | Connected speech rhythm                                  | PPJ workplace example                   | Rapid fire trigger     |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| The issue **may be related to** a missing carton.           | Vấn đề có thể liên quan đến một thùng hàng bị thiếu.                | The issue may be reLAted / to a missing carton.          | Kho nhận thiếu một carton.              | Có thể thiếu carton.   |\n| It happened because the supplier **used an old document.**  | Việc này xảy ra vì supplier sử dụng chứng từ cũ.                    | It happened beCAUSE / the supplier used an old document. | Supplier gửi packing list phiên bản cũ. | Supplier dùng file cũ. |\n| We **cannot confirm the cause** until we check the records. | Chúng tôi chưa thể xác nhận nguyên nhân cho đến khi kiểm tra hồ sơ. | We can’t confirm the CAUSE / until we check the records. | Chưa đủ dữ liệu để kết luận.            | Chưa rõ nguyên nhân.   |\n\n  \n\nFUNCTION C: EXPLAIN THE IMPACT AND STATUS\n\n| Complete expression                                                      | Meaning in Vietnamese                                        | Connected speech rhythm                                      | PPJ workplace example              | Rapid fire trigger           |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| **As a result**, **we cannot complete** + (n) the receiving process yet. | Vì vậy, chúng tôi chưa thể hoàn tất quy trình nhận hàng.     | As a reSULT / we can’t complete / the receiving process yet. | Kho chưa thể hoàn tất receiving.   | Chưa thể hoàn tất receiving. |\n| The issue may **delay the shipment update.**                             | Vấn đề có thể làm chậm việc cập nhật lô hàng.                | The issue may deLAY / the shipment update.                   | XNK chưa thể báo status chính xác. | Có thể chậm shipment update. |\n| **We are currently** checking the cartons and documents.                 | Hiện tại chúng tôi đang kiểm tra các thùng hàng và chứng từ. | We’re currently CHECKing / the cartons and documents.        | Kho đang kiểm đếm lại.             | Đang kiểm tra.               |\n\nFUNCTION D: PROPOSE THE NEXT ACTION\n\n| Complete expression                                              | Meaning in Vietnamese                                   | Connected speech rhythm                                        | PPJ workplace example                  | Rapid fire trigger         |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| **Could you** *contact the supplier and confirm the quantity?*   | Bạn có thể liên hệ supplier và xác nhận số lượng không? | Could you CONtact the supplier / and confirm the quantity?     | XNK cần hỏi supplier số lượng đã gửi.  | Nhờ xác nhận với supplier. |\n| Let’s **cross-check the documents** before we update the system. | Hãy kiểm tra chéo chứng từ trước khi cập nhật hệ thống. | Let’s cross-check the DOCuments / before we update the system. | PO, invoice và packing list khác nhau. | Kiểm tra trước khi update. |\n| **I’ll send another update** when we have more information.      | Tôi sẽ gửi cập nhật khác khi có thêm thông tin.         | I’ll send another UPdate / when we have more information.      | Chưa có kết quả cuối cùng.             | Sẽ cập nhật thêm.          |\n\n4. RAPID FIRE PRACTICE\n\nBạn nghe trigger tiếng Việt và trả lời trong 5 giây.\n\n|Trigger|Complete response|\n|---|---|\n|Có chênh lệch số lượng|We found a quantity difference in today’s delivery.|\n|Chứng từ có vấn đề|There seems to be an issue with the shipment documents.|\n|System không khớp report|The information in the system does not match the report.|\n|Có thể thiếu carton|The issue may be related to a missing carton.|\n|Supplier dùng file cũ|It happened because the supplier used an old document.|\n|Chưa rõ nguyên nhân|We cannot confirm the cause until we check the records.|\n|Chưa thể hoàn tất receiving|As a result, we cannot complete the receiving process yet.|\n|Có thể chậm shipment update|The issue may delay the shipment update.|\n|Đang kiểm tra|We are currently checking the cartons and documents.|\n|Nhờ xác nhận với supplier|Could you contact the supplier and confirm the quantity?|\n|Kiểm tra trước khi update|Let’s cross-check the documents before we update the system.|\n|Sẽ cập nhật thêm|I’ll send another update when we have more information.|\n\n  \n\n5. THREE SPEAKING PATTERNS\n\nPATTERN 1: STATE THE PROBLEM WITH FACTS\n\nFramework\n\nWe found a problem with + document, quantity or system.\n\n  \n\nThe document shows + expected information.\n\n  \n\nHowever, the actual information is + actual information.\n\nSample answer\n\nWe found a problem with the received quantity. The packing list shows 500 pieces. However, the actual received quantity is 480 pieces.\n\nBUILD YOUR ANSWER\n\n|Information|Your notes|\n|---|---|\n|Problem||\n|Expected information||\n|Actual information||\n\nSay your answer to your partner.\n\nYour partner asks:\n\nWhen did you find the problem?\n\nAdd the time to your explanation.\n\nPATTERN 2: EXPLAIN THE CAUSE AND IMPACT\n\nFramework\n\nThe issue may be related to + possible cause.\n\n  \n\nAs a result, + business impact.\n\n  \n\nWe cannot + affected task yet.\n\nSample answer\n\nThe issue may be related to one missing carton. As a result, the received quantity does not match the packing list. We cannot complete the receiving process yet.\n\nBUILD YOUR ANSWER\n\n|Information|Your notes|\n|---|---|\n|Possible cause||\n|Business impact||\n|Affected task||\n\nSay your answer twice.\n\nRound 1: Use your notes.\n\nRound 2: Speak without reading the complete framework.\n\nPATTERN 3: GIVE A COMPLETE ISSUE UPDATE\n\nFramework\n\nThe main issue is + problem.\n\n  \n\nIt happened because or may be related to + cause.\n\n  \n\nAs a result, + impact.\n\n  \n\nWe are currently + status.\n\n  \n\nThe next step is to + action.\n\n  \n\nI’ll update you again by + time.\n\nSample answer\n\nThe main issue is a quantity difference in today’s delivery. It may be related to one missing carton. As a result, Warehouse cannot complete the receiving process. We are currently checking the cartons and delivery documents. The next step is to contact the supplier and confirm the shipped quantity. I’ll update you again by two p.m.\n\nBUILD YOUR ANSWER\n\n|Part|Your notes|\n|---|---|\n|Main issue||\n|Cause||\n|Impact||\n|Current status||\n|Next action||\n|Next update time||\n\nGive a 60 to 90 second issue update to your partner.\n\n6. TRANSFORM THE SENTENCES\n\nChange each unclear, emotional or blaming statement into a factual and collaborative explanation.\n\n|Unclear or blaming statement|Your professional version|\n|---|---|\n|The supplier made a mistake.||\n|The shipment is wrong.||\n|Warehouse lost the goods.||\n|Accounting entered the wrong number.||\n|IT has not fixed the system.||\n|The documents are a mess.||\n|We cannot do anything.||\n|This problem is not our responsibility.||\n|Someone used the wrong file.||\n|Everything is delayed now.||\n\nUSE THIS CHECKLIST\n\nA strong transformation should include at least three elements.\n\n□ A clear fact  \n□ A possible cause  \n□ A business impact  \n□ A current status  \n□ A next action  \n□ No personal blame\n\nMODEL TRANSFORMATION\n\nBlaming\n\nThe supplier sent the wrong document.\n\nProfessional\n\nThe document we received does not match the latest PO. The issue may be related to an older file version. We are checking the document history and will ask the supplier to send the updated version.\n\n7. ROLEPLAY: QUANTITY DIFFERENCE IN A DELIVERY\n\nSITUATION\n\nWarehouse receives a delivery for PO 6725.\n\n|Information|Details|\n|---|---|\n|Quantity on the packing list|1,000 pieces|\n|Quantity received|960 pieces|\n|Difference|40 pieces|\n|Possible cause|One carton may be missing|\n|Current status|Warehouse is recounting the goods|\n|Business impact|GRN cannot be completed|\n|Required action|XNK must contact the supplier|\n|Next internal update|Before 3:00 p.m.|\n\n  \n  \n\nROLE A: WAREHOUSE\n\nYou found the quantity difference.\n\nExplain:\n\n1. what the packing list shows;\n    \n2. what Warehouse received;\n    \n3. the possible cause;\n    \n4. how the issue affects the receiving process;\n    \n5. what Warehouse is doing now;\n    \n6. what you need from XNK.\n    \n\nUse at least five expressions.\n\nWe found a quantity difference in today’s delivery.\n\nThe packing list shows 1,000 pieces, but we received 960 pieces.\n\nThe issue may be related to one missing carton.\n\nAs a result, we cannot complete the GRN yet.\n\nWe are currently recounting the goods.\n\nCould you contact the supplier and confirm the shipped quantity?\n\nROLE B: IMPORT EXPORT\n\nYou need clear information before contacting the supplier.\n\nAsk:\n\n1. when the goods arrived;\n    \n2. whether all cartons were checked;\n    \n3. whether the packing list is the latest version;\n    \n4. what information the supplier needs to confirm;\n    \n5. when Warehouse can give the recount result.\n    \n\nUse at least five expressions.\n\nWhen did the delivery arrive?\n\nHave you checked all the cartons?\n\nIs this the latest version of the packing list?\n\nWhat quantity should I confirm with the supplier?\n\nWhen can you complete the recount?\n\nI’ll contact the supplier and send you an update before three p.m.  \n\nCONVERSATION FLOW\n\nState the problem\n\n→ Give the numbers\n\n→ Ask clarification questions\n\n→ Explain the possible cause\n\n→ Explain the impact\n\n→ Give the current status\n\n→ Agree on the next action\n\n→ Confirm the update time\n\nFINAL ISSUE SUMMARY\n\nComplete the summary together.\n\n|Item|Agreed information|\n|---|---|\n|The main problem is||\n|The expected quantity is||\n|The received quantity is||\n|The possible cause is||\n|Warehouse is currently||\n|Import–Export will||\n|The next update will be before||\n\nSUCCESS CHECK\n\n□ I explained the problem with clear facts.  \n□ I gave the expected and actual numbers.  \n□ I explained a possible cause without blaming anyone.  \n□ I described the business impact.  \n□ I gave the current status.  \n□ I proposed or accepted a next action.  \n□ We agreed on the next update time.\n\n8. SESSION TAKEAWAY\n\nA clear work problem explanation should not be:\n\nThe shipment is wrong, and the supplier made a mistake.\n\nUse this structure:\n\nProblem\n\n+\n\nCause\n\n+\n\nImpact\n\n+\n\nCurrent status\n\n+\n\nNext action\n\nFIVE SENTENCES TO REMEMBER\n\nWe found a quantity difference in today’s delivery.\n\nThe issue may be related to a missing carton.\n\nAs a result, we cannot complete the receiving process yet.\n\nWe are currently checking the cartons and documents.\n\nCould you contact the supplier and confirm the quantity?\n\nFINAL MESSAGE\n\nExplain the facts, show the impact and move the conversation toward a solution.\n\n  \n**","x":13240,"y":9760,"width":920,"height":20093},
		{"id":"5783f6d34b543abd","type":"text","text":"/id/ - t, d\n/t/ - \n/d/ - ","x":13000,"y":13580,"width":111,"height":120},
		{"id":"aaa0feca679155c4","type":"text","text":"homework2: transform 5 sentences of your choosing -> collaborative","x":12960,"y":16980,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"28b589a83181d639","type":"text","text":"homework 1: read aloud and record back ","x":13100,"y":10240,"width":140,"height":120},
		{"id":"cd619fdfd753d669","type":"text","text":"HOMEWORK 1 - FINISH THE EXERCISE ABOUT P.S + PP IN THE WORKSHEET","x":12980,"y":5980,"width":269,"height":117},
		{"id":"7883e47d7307a136","type":"text","text":"homework 1: hoan thanh viet lai cau - worksheet grammar - tenses","x":8800,"y":11220,"width":250,"height":86},
		{"id":"0dca002e75cae8d6","type":"text","text":"EXPLAIN:\n- S + NEED + OBJECT + TO DO SOMETHING \n- S + TO-BE(AM/IS/ARE - WAS/WERE - BEEN) + WAITING + FOR + OBJECT + TO DO SMTHING\n","x":8860,"y":15000,"width":220,"height":260},
		{"id":"f12a8cacaebf7fd5","type":"text","text":"CHECK CURRENT STATS:\n- DO YOU HAVE ANY UPDATE ON + ...\n- COULD YOU UPDATE ME ON + ....","x":8870,"y":14600,"width":210,"height":220},
		{"id":"a44c7311d720dd67","type":"text","text":"Follow up:\n- Just checking in on\n- I'm following up on ","x":8870,"y":14300,"width":210,"height":125},
		{"id":"25e255c525c1c0d4","type":"text","text":"TIME- ARRANGING + CLOSE:\n\n- COULD YOU PLEASE UPDATE + SOMEBODY + BY + TIME ?\n- WHEN CAN WE / I EXPECT + OBJECT?","x":8860,"y":15300,"width":220,"height":240},
		{"id":"a3bcc42b181cde8b","type":"text","text":"homework 2: record + submit your reading of passage ->>","x":8700,"y":11400,"width":250,"height":89},
