		{"id":"515adcc81083fca6","x":14580,"y":9900,"width":840,"height":20093,"type":"text","text":"PPJ BUSINESS ENGLISH SPEAKING & LISTENING\n\nSESSION 9: MISTAKES, RESPONSIBILITY & SOLUTIONS\n\nLevel: A1–A2  \nWorkplace theme: Mistakes, responsibility and problem solving  \nSpeaking outcome: Bạn có thể nói về sai sót một cách bình tĩnh, nhận trách nhiệm phù hợp và đề xuất cách xử lý mà không đổ lỗi cho người khác.\n\nTODAY I CAN\n\n□ I can explain what went wrong.  \n□ I can acknowledge a mistake professionally.  \n□ I can avoid blaming another person or department.  \n□ I can explain what I am checking now.  \n□ I can suggest a clear solution.  \n□ I can confirm the next action and update time.\n\n1. READING\n\n**From a Mistake to a Solution**\n\nLan works in the Finance and Accounting Department. On Thursday morning, she checks a supplier invoice in the system. The invoice shows 580 pieces, but the purchase order shows 850 pieces.\n\nLan first thinks that Warehouse entered the wrong quantity. She wants to write:\n\n“Warehouse entered the wrong number. Please fix it.”\n\nHowever, Lan has not checked all the information yet. Her message may sound blaming and could create tension between the departments.\n\nLan contacts Warehouse and says:\n\n“There seems to be a quantity difference between the invoice and the PO. I may have used an older document, so I’m checking the file history now. Could you help me confirm the actual received quantity?”\n\nWarehouse checks the receiving record. The actual quantity is 580 pieces. The supplier used an old PO number on the invoice.\n\nLan then gives an update:\n\n“We found the cause of the difference. The supplier used an old PO reference. I’ll contact the supplier and ask for a corrected invoice. We can continue the payment process after we receive the new document.”\n\nLan does not hide the problem or blame another department. She checks the facts, explains the cause and moves the conversation toward a solution.\n\nNEW VOCABULARY\n\n|Word or phrase|Meaning in Vietnamese|\n|---|---|\n|mistake|sai sót|\n|responsibility|trách nhiệm|\n|take responsibility|nhận trách nhiệm|\n|blame|đổ lỗi|\n|incorrect|không chính xác|\n|quantity difference|chênh lệch số lượng|\n|file history|lịch sử file|\n|receiving record|hồ sơ nhận hàng|\n|old reference|mã tham chiếu cũ|\n|corrected invoice|hóa đơn đã chỉnh sửa|\n|solve the issue|giải quyết vấn đề|\n|prevent|ngăn ngừa|\n|next action|hành động tiếp theo|\n|happen again|xảy ra lần nữa|\n\nMULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS\n\n1. What problem does Lan find?\n\nA. The supplier has not sent the invoice.  \nB. The invoice and PO show different quantities.  \nC. Warehouse has lost the goods.  \nD. The system is not working.\n\n2. Why does Lan avoid blaming Warehouse?\n\nA. She does not know anyone in Warehouse.  \nB. She has not checked all the facts yet.  \nC. The invoice is not important.  \nD. Warehouse cannot change the information.\n\n3. What is the actual received quantity?\n\nA. 500 pieces  \nB. 580 pieces  \nC. 800 pieces  \nD. 850 pieces\n\n4. What caused the problem?\n\nA. Finance entered the wrong payment amount.  \nB. Warehouse used the wrong receiving record.  \nC. The supplier used an old PO reference.  \nD. The shipment arrived late.\n\n5. What does Lan do next?\n\nA. She cancels the payment.  \nB. She asks Warehouse to change the quantity.  \nC. She asks the supplier for a corrected invoice.  \nD. She creates a new purchase order.\n\n2. TONE LADDER\n\n**LEVEL 1: BLAMING OR UNPROFESSIONAL**\n\nYou entered the wrong number.\n\nThis is Warehouse’s mistake.\n\nThe supplier always sends incorrect documents.\n\nThis problem is not my responsibility.\n\nThese statements may create tension because they focus on the person instead of the problem.\n\n**LEVEL 2: POLITE AND FACTUAL**\n\nThere seems to be a quantity difference.\n\nThe invoice does not match the PO.\n\nWe need to check which document is correct.\n\nThese statements describe the facts without blaming anyone.\n\n**LEVEL 3: COLLABORATIVE AND SOLUTION FOCUSED**\n\nThere seems to be a quantity difference between the invoice and the PO.\n\nI may have used an older document, so I’m checking the file history now.\n\nCould you help me confirm the actual received quantity?\n\nAfter we confirm the cause, we can ask the supplier to correct the invoice.\n\nSOLUTION FOCUSED FLOW\n\nAcknowledge the issue\n\n→ Check the facts\n\n→ Explain the cause\n\n→ Take responsibility\n\n→ Suggest a solution\n\n→ Prevent the problem from happening again\n\nCOMPLETE MODEL\n\nThere seems to be a quantity difference between the invoice and the PO. I may have used an older document, so I’m checking the file history now. Could you help me confirm the actual received quantity? After that, I’ll contact the supplier and ask for a corrected invoice. I’ll update you again before three p.m.\n\n3. EXPRESSION BANK\n\nFUNCTION A: ACKNOWLEDGE THE MISTAKE\n\n|Complete expression|Meaning in Vietnamese|Connected speech rhythm|PPJ workplace example|Rapid fire trigger|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|It looks like there is a mistake in the report.|Có vẻ như có một sai sót trong báo cáo.|It looks like / there’s-a misTAKE / in-the-report.|Số lượng trong report không khớp WFX.|Báo cáo có sai sót.|\n|I may have missed an important detail.|Có thể tôi đã bỏ sót một chi tiết quan trọng.|I-may-have MISSED / an-important-detail.|Bạn chưa kiểm tra phiên bản mới nhất của file.|Có thể tôi bỏ sót.|\n|I’m sorry about the confusion.|Tôi xin lỗi về sự nhầm lẫn này.|I’m SORry / about-the-confusion.|Thông tin bạn gửi khiến phòng ban khác hiểu nhầm.|Xin lỗi vì nhầm lẫn.|\n\nFUNCTION B: CHECK WHAT HAPPENED\n\n|Complete expression|Meaning in Vietnamese|Connected speech rhythm|PPJ workplace example|Rapid fire trigger|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Let’s check what happened before we make any changes.|Hãy kiểm tra chuyện gì đã xảy ra trước khi thay đổi.|Let’s CHECK what-happened / before-we-make-any-changes.|Chưa biết PO hay invoice đúng.|Kiểm tra trước khi sửa.|\n|We need to confirm which document is correct.|Chúng ta cần xác nhận chứng từ nào là đúng.|We-need-to-conFIRM / which-document-is-correct.|Hai file có số lượng khác nhau.|Xác nhận file đúng.|\n|I’m checking the file history now.|Hiện tại tôi đang kiểm tra lịch sử file.|I’m CHECKing / the-file-history-now.|Có thể team đã dùng phiên bản cũ.|Đang kiểm tra lịch sử file.|\n\nFUNCTION C: TAKE RESPONSIBILITY PROFESSIONALLY\n\n|Complete expression|Meaning in Vietnamese|Connected speech rhythm|PPJ workplace example|Rapid fire trigger|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|I should have checked the latest version first.|Lẽ ra tôi nên kiểm tra phiên bản mới nhất trước.|I-should-have CHECKED / the-latest-version-first.|Bạn dùng file cũ để cập nhật report.|Lẽ ra nên kiểm tra trước.|\n|I’ll take responsibility for correcting the report.|Tôi sẽ chịu trách nhiệm chỉnh sửa báo cáo.|I’ll-take-responsiBILity / for-correcting-the-report.|Bạn cần cập nhật lại số liệu.|Tôi sẽ sửa báo cáo.|\n|I’ll make sure the information is updated correctly.|Tôi sẽ đảm bảo thông tin được cập nhật chính xác.|I’ll-make SURE / the-information-is-updated-correctly.|Bạn sẽ sửa dữ liệu trên system.|Đảm bảo update đúng.|\n\n  \n\nFUNCTION D: PROPOSE A SOLUTION\n\n|Complete expression|Meaning in Vietnamese|Connected speech rhythm|PPJ workplace example|Rapid fire trigger|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Here’s how we can fix the issue.|Đây là cách chúng ta có thể xử lý vấn đề.|Here’s-how-we-can FIX / the-issue.|Bạn bắt đầu trình bày phương án xử lý.|Đây là cách xử lý.|\n|I’ll contact the supplier and request a corrected invoice.|Tôi sẽ liên hệ supplier và yêu cầu hóa đơn điều chỉnh.|I’ll-CONtact-the-supplier / and-request-a-corrected-invoice.|Invoice sử dụng PO reference cũ.|Xin invoice mới.|\n|We should add one more checking step to prevent this from happening again.|Chúng ta nên thêm một bước kiểm tra để tránh lặp lại.|We-should-add / one-more-CHECKing-step / to-prevent-this-from-happening-again.|Team muốn ngăn lỗi file version.|Ngăn lỗi lặp lại.|\n\n4. RAPID FIRE PRACTICE\n\nBạn nghe trigger tiếng Việt và trả lời trong 5 giây.\n\n|Trigger|Complete response|\n|---|---|\n|Báo cáo có sai sót|It looks like there is a mistake in the report.|\n|Có thể tôi bỏ sót|I may have missed an important detail.|\n|Xin lỗi vì nhầm lẫn|I’m sorry about the confusion.|\n|Kiểm tra trước khi sửa|Let’s check what happened before we make any changes.|\n|Xác nhận file đúng|We need to confirm which document is correct.|\n|Đang kiểm tra lịch sử file|I’m checking the file history now.|\n|Lẽ ra nên kiểm tra trước|I should have checked the latest version first.|\n|Tôi sẽ sửa báo cáo|I’ll take responsibility for correcting the report.|\n|Đảm bảo update đúng|I’ll make sure the information is updated correctly.|\n|Đây là cách xử lý|Here’s how we can fix the issue.|\n|Xin invoice mới|I’ll contact the supplier and request a corrected invoice.|\n|Ngăn lỗi lặp lại|We should add one more checking step to prevent this from happening again.|\n\n5. THREE SPEAKING PATTERNS\n\nPATTERN 1: ACKNOWLEDGE AND CHECK\n\nFramework\n\nIt looks like there is a mistake in + document or system.\n\n  \n\nI may have + possible mistake.\n\n  \n\nI’m checking + information now.\n\nSample answer\n\nIt looks like there is a mistake in the payment report. I may have used an older invoice. I’m checking the document history now.\n\nBUILD YOUR ANSWER\n\n|Information|Your notes|\n|---|---|\n|Document or system||\n|Possible mistake||\n|Information you are checking||\n\nSay your answer to your partner.\n\nYour partner asks:\n\nWhen can you confirm the correct information?\n\nAdd a clear update time.\n\nPATTERN 2: TAKE RESPONSIBILITY AND FIX THE ISSUE\n\nFramework\n\nI should have + correct action.\n\n  \n\nI’ll take responsibility for + correction.\n\n  \n\nI’ll complete the correction by + time.\n\nSample answer\n\nI should have checked the latest file first. I’ll take responsibility for correcting the report. I’ll complete the correction by two p.m.\n\nBUILD YOUR ANSWER\n\n|Information|Your notes|\n|---|---|\n|What you should have done||\n|What you will correct||\n|Completion time||\n\nSay your complete answer twice.\n\nRound 1: Use your notes.\n\nRound 2: Speak without reading the framework.\n\nPATTERN 3: COMPLETE SOLUTION UPDATE\n\nFramework\n\nThe issue is + problem.\n\n  \n\nIt happened because + cause.\n\n  \n\nI may have or our team may have + responsibility.\n\n  \n\nHere’s how we can fix it.\n\n  \n\nFirst, we will + action one.\n\n  \n\nThen, we will + action two.\n\n  \n\nTo prevent this from happening again, we will + prevention.\n\nSample answer\n\nThe issue is an incorrect quantity in the payment report. It happened because the supplier used an old PO reference. I may have missed the difference during the first check. Here’s how we can fix it. First, I’ll ask the supplier for a corrected invoice. Then, I’ll update the report. To prevent this from happening again, we’ll check the PO reference before processing each invoice.\n\nBUILD YOUR ANSWER\n\n|Part|Your notes|\n|---|---|\n|Problem||\n|Cause||\n|Responsibility||\n|Action one||\n|Action two||\n|Prevention||\n\nGive a 60 to 90 second solution update to your partner.\n\n6. TRANSFORM THE SENTENCES\n\nChange each blaming or unprofessional sentence into a factual, responsible and solution focused statement.\n\n|Blaming or unprofessional sentence|Your professional version|\n|---|---|\n|You entered the wrong quantity.||\n|This is Warehouse’s mistake.||\n|Accounting did not check the invoice.||\n|The supplier always sends bad documents.||\n|IT caused the whole problem.||\n|This is not my responsibility.||\n|Someone used the wrong file again.||\n|You need to fix this now.||\n|We cannot continue because of your mistake.||\n|This problem keeps happening because nobody checks anything.||\n\nUSE THIS CHECKLIST\n\nA strong transformation should include at least three elements.\n\n□ A clear fact  \n□ No personal blame  \n□ A possible cause  \n□ Appropriate responsibility  \n□ A solution  \n□ A prevention step\n\nMODEL TRANSFORMATION\n\nBlaming\n\nWarehouse entered the wrong number.\n\nProfessional\n\nThe quantity in the system does not match the receiving record. We need to confirm which number is correct. After that, I’ll update the report and inform the related teams.\n\n7. ROLEPLAY: WRONG QUANTITY ENTERED IN THE SYSTEM\n\nSITUATION\n\nA quantity was entered incorrectly in the system for PO 7730.\n\n|Information|Details|\n|---|---|\n|Actual received quantity|720 pieces|\n|Quantity in the system|270 pieces|\n|Person who entered the data|Warehouse staff member|\n|Possible cause|The digits were entered in the wrong order|\n|Business impact|Finance cannot complete the invoice check|\n|Current action|Warehouse is checking the receiving record|\n|Required correction|Update the system quantity to 720|\n|Next update|Before 2:30 p.m.|\n\n  \n  \n\nROLE A: FINANCE AND ACCOUNTING\n\nYou found the difference while checking the supplier invoice.\n\nYou need to:\n\n1. explain the difference without blaming Warehouse;\n    \n2. ask Warehouse to confirm the actual quantity;\n    \n3. explain the impact on invoice checking;\n    \n4. ask when the system can be corrected;\n    \n5. confirm the next action.\n    \n\nUse at least five sentences.\n\nThere seems to be a quantity difference in the system.\n\nThe invoice shows 720 pieces, but the system shows 270 pieces.\n\nCould you help me confirm the actual received quantity?\n\nWe cannot complete the invoice check until the quantity is confirmed.\n\nWhen can the system information be corrected?\n\nPlease send me an update when the correction is complete.\n\nROLE B: WAREHOUSE\n\nYou entered the quantity into the system.\n\nYou discover that the digits were entered in the wrong order.\n\nYou need to:\n\n1. acknowledge the mistake;\n    \n2. explain what happened;\n    \n3. take responsibility for correcting it;\n    \n4. give a completion time;\n    \n5. suggest a prevention step.\n    \n\nUse at least five sentences.\n\nIt looks like I entered the digits in the wrong order.\n\nI’m sorry about the confusion.\n\nI should have checked the quantity before saving the record.\n\nI’ll take responsibility for correcting the system information.\n\nI can complete the correction before two thirty.\n\nWe should add a second check before saving quantity data.  \n\nCONVERSATION FLOW\n\nState the difference\n\n→ Ask for confirmation\n\n→ Check what happened\n\n→ Acknowledge the mistake\n\n→ Explain the business impact\n\n→ Agree on the correction\n\n→ Confirm the update time\n\n→ Suggest a prevention step\n\nFINAL AGREEMENT\n\nComplete the summary together.\n\n|Item|Agreed information|\n|---|---|\n|The actual quantity is||\n|The system quantity is||\n|The cause of the mistake is||\n|Warehouse will||\n|Finance will continue after||\n|The correction will be completed by||\n|To prevent the problem, the team will||\n\nSUCCESS CHECK\n\n□ I described the facts without blaming anyone.  \n□ I acknowledged the mistake professionally.  \n□ I explained what caused the mistake.  \n□ I accepted an appropriate level of responsibility.  \n□ I proposed a clear correction.  \n□ We agreed on a completion time.  \n□ We suggested a prevention step.\n\n8. SESSION TAKEAWAY\n\nProfessional responsibility does not mean:\n\nEverything is my fault.\n\nIt means:\n\nAcknowledge the issue\n\n+\n\nCheck the facts\n\n+\n\nAccept your part\n\n+\n\nCorrect the problem\n\n+\n\nPrevent it from happening again\n\nFIVE SENTENCES TO REMEMBER\n\nIt looks like there is a mistake in the report.\n\nI may have missed an important detail.\n\nLet’s check what happened before we make any changes.\n\nI’ll take responsibility for correcting the information.\n\nWe should add one more checking step to prevent this from happening again.\n\nFINAL MESSAGE\n\nFocus less on who made the mistake and more on how the team can correct it.\n\nNội dung được phát triển theo mục tiêu Session 9 trong course master plan: chuyển từ blame language sang solution language và xử lý tình huống sai số lượng trên hệ thống.\n\n  \n**"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"c8a8cd88be3304b9","fromNode":"1f2053a511f45bf3","fromSide":"right","toNode":"5d9284e604f46d64","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"c3fec377fee52f34","fromNode":"1be102effa7fb81b","fromSide":"right","toNode":"1f2053a511f45bf3","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"a10814ed2d811213","fromNode":"5d9284e604f46d64","fromSide":"right","toNode":"f948dd9036679f2a","toSide":"left"},
